[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the given problem, we need to find a second-degree polynomial \( p(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \) that satisfies the conditions \( p(1) = 1 \), \( p(2) = 3 \), and \( p(3) = 2 \). Additionally, we need to verify that \( p(p(x)) = x \) has four real solutions and determine which of these solutions is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's set up the system of equations using the given conditions:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a(1)^2 + b(1) + c = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a(2)^2 + b(2) + c = 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a(3)^2 + b(3) + c = 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a + b + c = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4a + 2b + c = 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9a + 3b + c = 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we subtract the first equation from the second and the second from the third to eliminate \( c \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (4a + 2b + c) - (a + b + c) = 3 - 1 \implies 3a + b = 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (9a + 3b + c) - (4a + 2b + c) = 2 - 3 \implies 5a + b = -1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we have a system of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3a + b = 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5a + b = -1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract the first equation from the second:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (5a + b) - (3a + b) = -1 - 2 \implies 2a = -3 \implies a = -\frac{3}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute \( a = -\frac{3}{2} \) back into \( 3a + b = 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3\left(-\frac{3}{2}\right) + b = 2 \implies -\frac{9}{2} + b = 2 \implies b = 2 + \frac{9}{2} = \frac{4}{2} + \frac{9}{2} = \frac{13}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the coefficients are \( a = -\frac{3}{2} \), \( b = \frac{13}{2} \), and \( c = -\frac{7}{2} \). The polynomial \( p(x) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m p(x) = -\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to verify that \( p(p(x)) = x \) has four real solutions. First, we find \( p(p(x)) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m p(p(x)) = p\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2}\right) = a\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2}\right)^2 + b\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2}\right) - \frac{7}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = -\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( p(p(x)) = x \) to have four real solutions, the equation \( -\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2} = x \) must have four solutions. This equation can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - \frac{7}{2} - x = 0 \implies -\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{11}{2}x - \frac{7}{2} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
