[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5a + b = -1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract the first equation from the second:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (5a + b) - (3a + b) = -1 - 2 \implies 2a = -3 \implies a = -\frac{3}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute \( a = -\frac{3}{2} \) into \( 3a + b = 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3\left(-\frac{3}{2}\right) + b = 2 \implies -\frac{9}{2} + b = 2 \implies b = 2 + \frac{9}{2} = \frac{13}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute \( a = -\frac{3}{2} \) and \( b = \frac{13}{2} \) back into \( a + b + c = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -\frac{3}{2} + \frac{13}{2} + c = 1 \implies \frac{10}{2} + c = 1 \implies 5 + c = 1 \implies c = -4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the polynomial \( p(x) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ p(x) = -\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 3: Find \( p(p(x)) \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute \( p(x) \) into \( p(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ p(p(x)) = p\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - 4\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, compute \( p\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - 4\right) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m p\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - 4\right) = -\frac{3}{2}\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - 4\right)^2 + \frac{13}{2}\left(-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \frac{13}{2}x - 4\right) - 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Distribute and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
