[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Factor out the common factor:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We can factor \((x+2)\) out of both terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    x(x+2) + (x+2) = (x + 2)(x + 2)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Here, \((x + 2)\) is the common factor that remains after both terms have been factored out.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the factored form of the expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{(x + 2)(x + 2)}
