[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(n) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n + 10 & \text{if } n < 10, \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m f(n - 5) & \text{if } n \ge 10.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \right.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This means that for \( n \ge 10 \), the function \( f(n) \) depends on what \( f(n - 5) \) is. We need to consider the value of \( f(q) \) for \( q \) from 10 to 1.1 (because \( f(n) \) for \( n < 10 \) is not specified, but we are looking for the maximum within the region and we assume this region is continuous). 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( q - 5 \ge 0 \), which means \( q \ge 5 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(q) = f(q - 5) = q + 10.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( q - 5 < 0 \), which means \( q < 5 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(q) = q.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m At the boundary \( n = 10 \), we need to check both sides of the function definition:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(10) = 10 + 10 = 20.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( n = 11 \), we need to check:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(11) = f(11 - 5) = f(6) = 6 + 10 = 16.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( n = 12 \), we need to check:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(12) = f(12 - 5) = f(7) = 7 + 10 = 17.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We observe that \( f(12) > f(11) \) and \( f(12) > f(10) \) except at the point where the function definition changes. To confirm, let's consider the pattern by examining the values for \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( n < 10 \), \( f(n) = n + 10 \), which increases as \( n \) increases.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( n = 10 \), \( f(10) = 20 \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \( n > 10 \), \( f(n) = f(n - 5) \), which decreases as \( n \) increases.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m From the above, it is clear that the maximum value of \( f(n) \) occurs at \( n = 11 \) where \( f(11) = 16 \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the maximum value of the function is \(\boxed{16}\).<|endoftext|>
