[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A right rectangular prism has a base area one-quarter the base area of a larger right rectangular prism. The height of the smaller prism is half the height of the larger one. What is the ratio of the volume of the smaller prism to the volume of the larger prism? Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the ratio of the volume of the smaller prism to the volume of the larger prism, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the volumes of the prisms:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Let \( V \) be the volume of the larger prism.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Let \( V_{\text{small}} \) be the volume of the smaller prism.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Express the volumes in terms of the base areas:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Let the base area of the larger prism be \( B \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The base area of the smaller prism is \( \frac{B}{4} \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Let the height of the larger prism be \( h \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Calculate the volume of the larger prism:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    V = B \cdot h
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Calculate the volume of the smaller prism:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    V_{\text{small}} = \left(\frac{B}{4}\right) \cdot h = \frac{Bh}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. **Find the ratio of the volumes:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Ratio} = \frac{V_{\text{small}}}{V} = \frac{\frac{Bh}{4}}{Bh} = \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the ratio of the volume of the smaller prism to the volume of the larger prism is \(\boxed{\frac{1}{4}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{1}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{1}{4}
