[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m What is the remainder when the product $1734\times 5389 \times 80,\!607$ is divided by 10?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the remainder when the product \(1734 \times 5389 \times 80,607\) is divided by 10, we can focus on the last digits of each of the numbers involved in the multiplication.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Identify the last digit of \(1734\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1734 \equiv 4 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Identify the last digit of \(5389\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    5389 \equiv 9 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Identify the last digit of \(80,607\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    80,607 \equiv 7 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we need to multiply these last digits together and then find the remainder when this product is divided by 10. First, multiply \(4\) and \(9\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4 \times 9 = 36
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The last digit of \(36\) is \(6\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, multiply \(36\) and \(7\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 36 \times 7 = 252
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The last digit of \(252\) is \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, the product of all the last digits is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 36 \times 7 = 252 \equiv 2 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the remainder when the product \(1734 \times 5389 \times 80,607\) is divided by 10 is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
