[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(x - 0) = \sqrt{f(x \cdot 0) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(x) = \sqrt{f(0) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we set \( x = y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(x - x) = \sqrt{f(x^2) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(0) = \sqrt{f(x^2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we set \( x = 2y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2y) = \sqrt{f(4y^2) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2y) = \sqrt{f(4y^2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we look at the function \( g(x) = f(x) + 2 \). Then for any \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(x - y) = \sqrt{f(xy) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We want to find \( f(2009) \). Setting \( x = 4999 \) and \( y = 2003 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(4999 - 2003) = \sqrt{f(4999 \cdot 2003) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2996) = \sqrt{f(9997077) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \( f \) is positive for all \( x > 0 \), the right side must be the square root of a positive number, so it must be positive. This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2996) = \sqrt{f(9997077) + 2} > 0. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since both sides are positive, the equality must hold. Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2996) = \sqrt{f(9997077) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2996)^2 = f(9997077) + 2. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m However, we can also use the equation \( f(2y) = \sqrt{f(4y^2) + 2} \) with \( x = y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2 \cdot y) = \sqrt{f(4y^2) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2y) = \sqrt{f(4y^2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Setting \( y = 2504 \) and \( x = 4999 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2 \cdot 4999) = \sqrt{f(4999^2) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(9998) = \sqrt{f(4999^2) + 2}. \]
