[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(9998) = \sqrt{f(4999^2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can continue this process, but we notice a pattern. By considering the functional equation more carefully, we can deduce that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2009) = \sqrt{f(2000^2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can use the equation \( f(x - y) = \sqrt{f(xy) + 2} \) with \( x = 2y \) and \( y = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2y - y) = \sqrt{f(2y^2) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(y) = \sqrt{f(2y^2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \( f \) is periodic with period 2, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(1) = \sqrt{f(1) + 2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2) = \sqrt{f(2) + 2}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m By continuing this process, we find:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(2009) = \sqrt{f(2998^2) + 2}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m and
