[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To round $54.\overline{54}$ to the nearest hundredth, we first identify the digit in the thousandths place. In this case, the digit in the thousandths place is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we look at the digit immediately to the right of the thousandths place. This digit, which is 4, is less than 5. Therefore, we stop the rounding process and simply round the digit in the hundredths place (which is the digit immediately to the right of the thousandths place). The digit in the hundredths place is 4.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m When we round 4 to the nearest hundredth, we move one place to the left, where it becomes 4.00.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, $54.\overline{54}$ rounded to the nearest hundredth is $\boxed{54.00}$.<|endoftext|>
