[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To rationalize the denominator of \(\frac{5}{\sqrt{3}}\), we need to eliminate the square root from the denominator. We do this by multiplying both the numerator and the denominator by \(\sqrt{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Start with the original fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{5}{\sqrt{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Multiply both the numerator and the denominator by \(\sqrt{3}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{5}{\sqrt{3}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Simplify the expression by multiplying the numerators together and the denominators together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{5 \cdot \sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3} \cdot \sqrt{3}} = \frac{5\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the rationalized form of the denominator is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{5\sqrt{3}}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
