[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m What is the product of the digits in the base 8 representation of $6543_{10}$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the product of the digits in the base 8 representation of \(6543_{10}\), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Convert the decimal number \(6543_{10}\) to its base 8 representation.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Identify the digits in the base 8 representation.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Calculate the product of these digits.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 1: Convert \(6543_{10}\) to base 8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To convert a decimal number to base 8, we repeatedly divide the number by 8 and keep track of the remainders.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{r|l}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6543 \div 8 & 1282 & 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{r|l}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1282 \div 8 & 160 & 7 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 160 \div 8 & 20 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 20 \div 8 & 2 & 8 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 \div 8 & 0 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base 8 representation of \(6543_{10}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6543_{10} = 48725_8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 2: Identify the digits in the base 8 representation
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The digits in the base 8 representation are \(4, 8, 7, 2, 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 3: Calculate the product of these digits
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to multiply these digits together:
