[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the measure of angle \( x \) in triangle \( ABC \) where \( AC = BC \) and \( \angle BAC = 40^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's analyze the triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Since \( AC = BC \), triangle \( ABC \) is isosceles with \( A = C \). Let's denote the angles at \( A \), \( B \), and \( C \) as \( \angle CAB = \angle BAC = 40^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. The sum of the interior angles in any triangle is always \( 180^\circ \). Therefore, for triangle \( ABC \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \angle BAC + \angle ABC + \angle ACB = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since \( \angle BAC = 40^\circ \), the remaining angles are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \angle CAB = 40^\circ \quad \text{and} \quad \angle ABC = \angle ACB = \theta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    40^\circ + \theta + \theta = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    40^\circ + 2\theta = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2\theta = 140^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \theta = 70^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Now, \( x \) is the angle at \( B \) (third vertex). So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \angle BAC + \angle BCA + \angle x = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since \( \angle BCA = \theta = 70^\circ \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    40^\circ + 70^\circ + \angle x = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    110^\circ + \angle x = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \angle x = 70^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the number of degrees in angle \( x \) is \(\boxed{70}\).<|endoftext|>
