[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The probability of rain tomorrow is $\frac{1}{11}$.  What is the probability that it will not rain tomorrow?  Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the probability that it will not rain tomorrow given that the probability of rain is \(\frac{1}{11}\), we need to consider the complement of the event that it will rain. Since the probability of rain is independent of the probability of no rain, we can use the fact that the sum of the probabilities of all possible outcomes must be 1.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let \(P(\text{rain}) = \frac{1}{11}\) be the probability of rain, and let \(P(\text{no rain})\) be the probability of not rain. The complement of the event that it will not rain (denoted as \(P(\text{no rain}|\text{not rain})\)) can be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[P(\text{no rain}|\text{not rain}) = 1 - P(\text{rain})\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(P(\text{rain}) = \frac{1}{11}\), we substitute this value into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[P(\text{no rain}|\text{not rain}) = 1 - \frac{1}{11} = \frac{11}{11} - \frac{1}{11} = \frac{10}{11}\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the probability that it will not rain tomorrow, expressed as a common fraction, is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\boxed{\frac{10}{11}}\]<|endoftext|>
