[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If $\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 0 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{B}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 3 \end{pmatrix},$ then find the inverse of $\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the inverse of \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\), we need to use the formula for the inverse of a product of two square matrices. The formula is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B})^{-1} = \mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{B}^{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We are given that \(\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 0 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{B}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 3 \end{pmatrix}\). To find \(\mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{B}^{-1}\), we multiply the matrices:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{B}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 0 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We perform the matrix multiplication on the left side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 0 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \cdot 2 + 0 \cdot (-1) & 4 \cdot (-1) + 0 \cdot 3 \\ 1 \cdot 2 + (-1) \cdot (-1) & 1 \cdot (-1) + (-1) \cdot 3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Calculating each element of the resulting matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 4 \cdot 2 + 0 \cdot (-1) & 4 \cdot (-1) + 0 \cdot 3 \\ 1 \cdot 2 + (-1) \cdot (-1) & 1 \cdot (-1) + (-1) \cdot 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -4 \\ 3 & -4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the inverse of \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 8 & -4 \\ 3 & -4 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
