[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The function $f$ is defined on positive integers as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[f(n) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n + 10 & \text{if $n < 10$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m f(n - 5) & \text{if $n \ge 10$}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \right.\]Find the maximum value of the function.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The maximum value of the function $f(n)$ can be determined by examining the definition of $f(n)$ for both $n < 10$ and $n \ge 10$. The floor function $\lfloor x \rfloor$ gives the largest integer less than or equal to $x$, and for any integer $n$, $f(n) = \lfloor n + 10 \rfloor$ if $n < 10$, and $f(n) = \lfloor n - 5 \rfloor$ if $n \ge 10$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Case 1:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For $n < 10$, the maximum value happens when $\lfloor n + 10 \rfloor$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \lfloor n + 10 \rfloor = \lfloor n \rfloor + 9.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the maximum value in this case is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \max \{\lfloor n \rfloor + 9 \mid n < 10\} = n + 9 .
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Case 2:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For $n \ge 10$, the maximum value happens when $\lfloor n - 5 \rfloor$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \lfloor n - 5 \rfloor = \lfloor n - 6 \rfloor = 6 .
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the maximum value in this case is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \max \{ \lfloor n - 5 \rfloor \mid n \ge 10\} = 6 .
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Hence, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n + 9 \le f(n) \le 6 \quad \text{for} \quad n \in \mathbb{Z}^+.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The largest possible value is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{9}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
