[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For each pair of real numbers $a \ne b$, define the operation $\star$ as \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (a \star b) = \frac{a + b}{a - b}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]What is the value of $((1 \star 2) \star 4)$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the problem \( ((1 \star 2) \star 4) \), we need to follow the definition of the operation \(\star\) given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (a \star b) = \frac{a + b}{a - b}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We will start by calculating \(1 \star 2\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 \star 2 = \frac{1 + 2}{1 - 2} = \frac{3}{-1} = -3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we use the result \(-3\) as the first argument in the next star operation, \( -3 \star 4 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
