[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Find the projection of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the formula for the projection of a vector \(\mathbf{u}\) onto a vector \(\mathbf{v}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{v}} \mathbf{u} = \left( \frac{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v}}{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{v}} \right) \mathbf{v}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Here, \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we need to compute the dot product \(\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v} = (1)(8) + (-2)(1) = 8 - 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we compute the dot product \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{v}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{v} = (8)(8) + (1)(1) = 64 + 1 = 65
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we can substitute these values into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{v}} \mathbf{u} = \left( \frac{6}{65} \right) \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{6 \cdot 8}{65} \\ \frac{6 \cdot 1}{65} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{48}{65} \\ \frac{6}{65} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
