[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify the expression \(\cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{6 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13}\), we will use properties of roots of unity and symmetry in the unit circle.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, recall that \(\omega = e^{2\pi i / 13}\) is a primitive 13th root of unity. This means that \(\omega^k = -1\) for \(k = 1, 2, \ldots, 12\), and \(\omega^{13} = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We start by considering the sum of cosines at specific angles around the unit circle. Notice that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos \frac{2\pi}{13} = \omega^1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos \frac{6\pi}{13} = \omega^2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos \frac{8\pi}{13} = \omega^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Adding these yields:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos \frac{2\pi}{13} + \cos \frac{6\pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8\pi}{13} = \omega^1 + \omega^2 + \omega^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we use the fact that \(\omega\) satisfies \(\omega^3 = 1\) and \(\omega^2 + 1 = 0\). Therefore, \(\omega^2 = -1 - \omega\) and \(\omega\) can be written as \(\omega = e^{2\pi i / 13}\). This means \(\omega^2 = -1 - \omega\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Rewriting the sum of cosines, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \omega^1 + \omega^2 + \omega^3 = e^{2\pi i / 13} + (-1 - \omega) + (-\omega)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m e^{2\pi i / 13} + (-1 - \omega) + (-\omega) = e^{2\pi i / 13}(-2 - \omega)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the simplified expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{e^{2\pi i / 13}(-2 - \omega)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
