[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let $P(x)$ be a polynomial such that when $P(x)$ is divided by $x - 19,$ the remainder is 99, and when $P(x)$ is divided by $x - 99,$ the remainder is 19.  What is the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $(x - 19)(x - 99)$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find the remainder when the polynomial \(P(x)\) is divided by \((x - 19)(x - 99)\). This means that the remainder must be a polynomial of degree less than 2, i.e., of the form \(ax + b\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. When \(P(x)\) is divided by \(x - 19\), the remainder is 99.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. When \(P(x)\) is divided by \(x - 99\), the remainder is 19.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can express these conditions using the polynomial division formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(x) = (x - 19)(x - 99)Q(x) + ax + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \(Q(x)\) is the quotient.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For a remainder of \(ax + b\), the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(x) = (x - 19)(x - 99)Q(x) + ax + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(x) - ax - b = (x - 19)(x - 99)Q(x) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This equation tells us that \(P(x) - ax - b\) must be divisible by both \(x - 19\) and \(x - 99\). Therefore, there exists some constant \(k\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(x) - ax - b = k(x - 19)(x - 99) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(P(x)\) is a polynomial of degree less than 2, it must be the same as \(ax + b\) because \(k\) must be zero (otherwise, it would not be a divisible polynomial). Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(x) = ax + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to determine \(b\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(x) = ax + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Evaluating at \(x = 19\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(19) = a(19) + b = 19a + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(P(19) = 99\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 19a + b = 99 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Evaluating at \(x = 99\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P(99) = a(99) + b = 99a + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(P(99) = 19\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 99a + b = 19 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We now has a system of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. \(19a + b = 99\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. \(99a + b = 19\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract the first equation from the second:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ (99a + b) - (19a + b) = 19 - 99 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 80a = -80 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ a = -1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute \(a = -1\) back into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 19(-1) + b = 99 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -19 + b = 99 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ b = 118 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the remainder when \(P(x)\) is divided by \((x - 19)(x - 99)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{118} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -x + 118
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
