[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many people will end up with fewer than 7 cards when 52 cards are dealt to 8 people as evenly as possible, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Calculate the average number of cards each person will receive.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Determine how many cards each person will have if they are given the average amount.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Identify how many people will have more than 7 cards.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Identify how many people will have fewer than 7 cards.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Step 1: Calculate the average number of cards each person will receive.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The total number of cards is 52, and they are being dealt to 8 people. So, the average number of cards each person will receive is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{52}{8} = 6.5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since we can only have whole cards, each person will receive either 6 or 7 cards.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Step 2: Determine how many cards each person will have if they are given the average amount.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If each person is given exactly 6 cards, they will each have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{6}{8} = 0.75
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since they each received 6 cards, and no one has more than 7 cards, all 0.75 cards are distributed to the 7 people who received 6 cards each. The remaining card will be given to one of the other 2 people.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Step 3: Identify how many people will have more than 7 cards.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Each of the 8 people who received 6 cards will have 6 cards, and each of the 6 people who received 7 cards will have 7 cards. Therefore, the 2 people who received 6 cards will have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 + 7 + 7 + 7 = 26
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Of these, 2 is fewer than 7 cards.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Step 4: Identify how many people will have fewer than 7 cards.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since we have 18 people receiving 6 cards and 2 receiving 6 cards, all 18 people will have fewer than 7 cards. The 2 people receiving 7 cards can be put into the remaining 2 people.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the number of people who will end up with fewer than 7 cards is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
