[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the given system of determinant equations, we need to find all values of \( x \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\ x & 7 & -2 \\ x^3 & 343 & -8 \end{vmatrix} = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's expand the determinant along the first row:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\ x & 7 & -2 \\ x^3 & 343 & -8 \end{vmatrix} = 1 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} 7 & -2 \\ 343 & -8 \end{vmatrix} - 1 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} x & -2 \\ x^3 & -8 \end{vmatrix} + 1 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} x & 7 \\ x^3 & 343 \end{vmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's calculate each of the 2x2 determinants:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 7 & -2 \\ 343 & -8 \end{vmatrix} = 7 \cdot (-8) - (-2) \cdot 343 = -56 + 686 = 630,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x & -2 \\ x^3 & -8 \end{vmatrix} = x \cdot (-8) - (-2) \cdot x^3 = -8x + 2x^3,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x & 7 \\ x^3 & 343 \end{vmatrix} = x \cdot 343 - 7 \cdot x^3 = 343x - 7x^3.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting these back into the expansion, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 \cdot 630 - 1 \cdot (-8x + 2x^3) + 1 \cdot (343x - 7x^3) = 630 + 8x - 2x^3 + 343x - 7x^3.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 630 + 8x + 343x - 7x^3 - 2x^3 = 630 + 351x - 9x^3.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We set the determinant equal to zero:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 630 + 351x - 9x^3 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Rearrange the equation to form a standard polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -9x^3 + 351x + 630 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve this cubic equation, we can use the Rational Root Theorem, which suggests that any rational solution of the polynomial equation \( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0 \) is a factor of the constant term \( d \) divided by a factor of the leading coefficient \( a \). Here, the constant term \( d \) is 630 and the leading coefficient \( a \) is -9. The possible rational roots are the factors of 630 divided by the factors of -9. The factors of 630 are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 3, \pm 5, \pm 6, \pm 7, \pm 9, \pm 10, \pm 14, \pm 15, \pm 21, \pm 25, \pm 30, \pm 42, \pm 56, \pm 63, \pm 70, \pm 90, \pm 105, \pm 126, \pm 140, \pm 189, \pm 210, \pm 315, \pm 630.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We test these possible roots by substituting them into the polynomial. Let's start with \( x = 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -9(2)^3 + 351(2) + 630 = -9(8) + 702 + 630 = -72 + 702 + 630 = 1300 \neq 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, let's try \( x = -\frac{3}{2} \):
