[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the equation \(16^3 \times 8^3 = 2^K\), we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Simplify the left side of the equation by using the property of exponents that states \(a^m \times a^n = a^{m+n}\). Here, \(16 = 2^4\), so we can rewrite \(16^3\) as \((2^4)^3 = 2^{4 \times 3} = 2^{12}\). The right side of the equation remains as it is since there is no variable \(K\) in the right side.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2^{12} \times 8^3 = 2^{12+3} = 2^{15}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So the equation now becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
