[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m As I understand, you want to find the angle \( \angle APB \) given certain conditions about \( \angle SRT \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given that \( PA \) is tangent to semicircle \( SAR \) and \( PB \) is tangent to semicircle \( RBT \), and that \( AS \) is 58 degrees and \( BT \) is 37 degrees, we need to determine \(\angle APB\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's understand that \(\angle SRT\) is an angle inscribed in a semicircle, which means it is a right angle. Thus, \( \angle SRT = 90^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \( PA \) is tangent to semicircle \( SAR \) and \( PB \) is tangent to semicircle \( RBT \), the measure of the angles formed at the points of tangency, which are the angles between the tangents and the radii, will be:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(\angle ARP = \angle PSA = 90^\circ\) (since \( PA \) is tangent to the small arc at \( A \) and \( \angle SRT = 90^\circ \))
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(\angle BPT = \angle RTA = 90^\circ\) (since \( PB \) is tangent to the large arc at \( B \) and \( \angle SRT = 90^\circ \))
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the angles \( \angle APB \), \( \angle PBR \), \( \angle APR \), and \( \angle BPT \) are all right angles. Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(\angle APB = 90^\circ\) (since \(\angle APB\) is composed of two right angles added together)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Work done on both arcs \( AS \) and the semicircle parts is 0, so the other two due to tangency do not affect our computation.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Hence, \(\angle APB = 90^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
