[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A convex pentagon has three right angles. The other two angles are congruent to each other. What is the measure, in degrees, of one of these other angles?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Of course! I can help with this problem. 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the problem, we need to understand the relationship between the angles of a pentagon and how they all relate to each other. A convex pentagon has three right angles, which means it has one right angle (90 degrees) and four right angles. The remaining three angles are congruent to each other since they are all right angles.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's assign a variable \( R \) to represent the right angle. Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Four right angles: \( 4R = 90^\circ \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - One right angle: \( R = 45^\circ \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the measure of one of the other two congruent angles, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a pentagon is \( 540^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The sum of all the angles in a pentagon is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 540^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know four of the angles are \( 90^\circ \) each and one angle is \( R = 45^\circ \). So, we can write the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4 \times 90^\circ + R + R + 90^\circ = 540^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting \( R = 45^\circ \) into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4 \times 90^\circ + 45^\circ + 45^\circ + 90^\circ = 540^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 360^\circ + 45^\circ + 45^\circ + 90^\circ = 540^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
