[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This confirms our values are consistent. Now, to find the measure of one of the other two congruent angles, we recognize that the sum of the remaining angles (which are each 45 degrees) plus \( 45^\circ \) equals \( 540^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 135^\circ + 45^\circ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to determine the measure of the other two congruent angles. We know:
