[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the expression \((-2)^{3} + (-2)^{2} + (-2)^{1} + 2^{1} + 2^{2} + 2^{3}\), we need to evaluate each term individually and then sum them up.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Calculate \((-2)^{3}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (-2)^{3} = -8
