[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many memos three typists can type in one day, we need to first find out the combined typing speed of four typists. We know that four typists can type a total of 600 memos in three days. Therefore, the combined typing speed of four typists is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Typing speed of four typists} = \frac{600 \text{ memos}}{3 \text{ days}} = 200 \text{ memos/day} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since four typists together can type 200 memos, we can find the typing speed of one single typist by dividing this by four:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Typing speed of one typist} = \frac{200 \text{ memos}}{4 \text{ typists}} = 50 \text{ memos/typist} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to find out how many memos three typists can type in one day. If one single typist can type 50 memos per day, then three typists can type:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Typing speed of three typists} = 3 \times 50 \text{ memos/day} = 150 \text{ memos/day} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the number of memos that three typists can type in one day is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
