[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many digits are in the base-7 representation of the decimal number \(956\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Convert the decimal number to base-7**.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Count the number of digits in the base-7 representation**.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 1: Convert the decimal number \(956\) to base-7
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To convert a decimal number to base-7, we repeatedly divide the number by 7 and keep track of the remainders.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m &956 \div 7 = 136 \text{ remainder } 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m &136 \div 7 = 19 \text{ remainder } 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m &19 \div 7 = 2 \text{ remainder } 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m &2 \div 7 = 0 \text{ remainder } 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base-7 representation of \(956\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 956_{10} = 2536_7
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 2: Count the number of digits
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The base-7 representation \(2536_7\) has 4 digits.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the number of digits in the base-7 representation of \(956\) is \(\boxed{4}\).<|endoftext|>
