[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For real numbers $t \neq 0,$ the point
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[(x,y) = \left( \frac{t + 1}{t}, \frac{t - 1}{t} \right)\]is plotted.  All the plotted points lie on what kind of curve?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (A) Line
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (B) Circle
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (C) Parabola
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (D) Ellipse
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (E) Hyperbola
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Enter the letter of the correct option.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
