[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many dollars Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Jeremy earns per room by the number of rooms he cleaned. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Identify the amount Jeremy earns per room: \(\frac{11}{2}\) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Identify the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned: \(\frac{7}{3}\) rooms.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Multiply the amount Jeremy earns per room by the number of rooms he cleaned to find out how much Steven owes him.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The calculation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{11}{2} \times \frac{7}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To multiply these fractions, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{11 \times 7}{2 \times 3} = \frac{77}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, Steven owes Jeremy \(\boxed{\frac{77}{6}}\) dollars.<|endoftext|>
