[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Solve the system of equations: $\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x-3y=101\\ x+y=132\end{array}\right.$. To solve the system of equations given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2x - 3y = 10 & \text{(Equation 1)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y = 13 & \text{(Equation 2)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m we can use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate one of the variables by manipulating the equations.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 1: Eliminate \( y \) by making the coefficients of \( y \) in both equations the same. We can do this by multiplying Equation 2 by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3(x + y) = 3 \cdot 13
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3x + 3y = 39 \quad \text{(Equation 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2x - 3y = 10 & \text{(Equation 1)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3x + 3y = 39 & \text{(Equation 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 2: Add Equation 1 and Equation 3 to eliminate \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (2x - 3y) + (3x + 3y) = 10 + 39
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5x = 49
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Solving for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \frac{49}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 3: Substitute \( x = \frac{49}{5} \) back into Equation 2 to solve for \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{49}{5} + y = 13
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To isolate \( y \), subtract \(\frac{49}{5}\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m y = 13 - \frac{49}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Convert 13 to a fraction with a denominator of 5:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 13 = \frac{65}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m y = \frac{65}{5} - \frac{49}{5} = \frac{16}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the solutions to the system of equations are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\left( \frac{49}{5}, \frac{16}{5} \right)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
