[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the number of real solutions to the equation \(\frac{x}{100} = \sin x\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function \(f(x) = \frac{x}{100} - \sin x\) on the real number line. The range of \(\sin x\) is \([-1, 1]\), so the function \(f(x)\) will achieve values from \(\frac{x}{100} - 1\) to \(\frac{x}{100} + 1\). It can take any value in the interval \([1 - \frac{x}{100}, 1 + \frac{x}{100}]\).
