[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the monic polynomial with roots \(2r_1\), \(2r_2\), and \(2r_3\), we start by noting that if \(r\) is the root of the original polynomial \(-x^3 + 3x^2 - 8 = 0\), then \(2r\) is the root of the new polynomial \(2x^3 - 6x^2 + 8 = 0\). Therefore, the polynomial whose roots are \(2r_1\), \(2r_2\), and \(2r_3\) is \(2^3 x^3 - 6x^2 + 8 = 8x^3 - 6x^2 + 8\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the monic polynomial is \(\boxed{8x^3 - 6x^2 + 8}\).<|endoftext|>
