[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The average age of the three Wilson children is 7 years. If the two younger children are 4 years old and 7 years old, how many years old is the oldest child?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the age of the oldest child, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. We know that the average age of the three Wilson children is 7 years.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. The two younger children are 4 years old and 7 years old.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. We can calculate the total sum of the ages of the three children by multiplying the average age by the number of children.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The total sum of the ages is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 7 \text{ years/child} \times 3 \text{ children} = 21 \text{ years} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. We know the ages of the two younger children:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 4 \text{ years} + 7 \text{ years} = 11 \text{ years} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. The total sum of the ages of the three children is 21 years. Since 11 years is how many elder children we have, we subtract this from the total sum to find the age of the oldest child:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 21 \text{ years} - 11 \text{ years} = 10 \text{ years} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the youngest child is 10 years old, and the oldest child is \boxed{10}.<|endoftext|>
