[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the value of \( k \) for the line passing through points \( A(9, 1) \), \( B(19, k) \), and \( C(7, 0) \), we need to find the equation of the line in the standard form of a line equation, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ y = mx + b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \( m \) is the slope of the line and \( b \) is the y-intercept or the y-coordinate of point \( C \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we calculate the slope \( m \) using the formula for the slope between two points \( (x_1, y_1) \) and \( (x_2, y_2) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ m = \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting the coordinates of points \( A \) and \( B \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ m = \frac{k - 1}{19 - 9} = \frac{k - 1}{10} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we use the point-slope form of the equation of a line to find the equation of the line. The point-slope form is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ y - y_1 = m(x - x_1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Using point \( C(7, 0) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ y - 0 = \frac{k - 1}{10}(x - 7) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ y = \frac{k - 1}{10}(x - 7) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the value of \( k \), we need to determine the y-intercept of the line. The y-intercept occurs when \( x = 0 \). Substituting \( x = 0 \) into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ y = \frac{k - 1}{10}(0 - 7) = -\frac{7(k - 1)}{10} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the y-intercept is \( -\frac{7(k - 1)}{10} \). Setting this equal to zero (since the line passes through the x-axis and the y-coordinate is zero):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -\frac{7(k - 1)}{10} = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 7(k - 1) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ k - 1 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ k = 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( k \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{1} \]<|endoftext|>
