[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \(\sin \left( -\frac{\pi}{2} \right)\), we need to use the properties of the sine function, particularly noting that the sine function is odd. That is, \(\sin(-x) = -\sin(x)\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
