[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The common difference \(d\) is the difference between consecutive terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ d = 85 - 88 = -3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The number \(-17\) can be expressed in the form \(88 - 3k\) for some integer \(k\). To find \(k\), we solve for \(k\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -17 = 88 - 3k \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -17 - 88 = -3k \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -105 = -3k \]
