[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. The total number of students in the school is 1200. Since one-half of the students are boys, we can calculate the number of boys as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Number of boys} = \frac{1}{2} \times 1200 = 600
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Now, we need to find two-thirds of the number of girls and one-half of the number of boys:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Number of girls attending the picnic} = \frac{2}{3} \times 800 = \frac{1600}{3} \approx 533.33
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since the number of students must be a whole number, we can assume the problem is intended to have an exact calculation or might involve rounding. However, for the exact calculation, we can use:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Number of girls attending the picnic} = 800
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Next, we subtract the number of boys from the sum of the number of girls and boys to find the number of girls attending the picnic:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
