[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Find the solutions to $z^3 = -8.$  Enter the solutions, separated by commas.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the solutions to \( z^3 = -8 \), we start by expressing \(-8\) in polar form. The number \(-8\) can be written as \(8 \text{cis}(\pi)\) or \(8 \text{cis}(-\pi)\), where \(\text{cis}(\theta) = \cos(\theta) + i\sin(\theta)\). Squaring this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ z^3 = 8^3 \text{cis}(3\pi). \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we calculate \(8^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 8^3 = 8 \cdot 8 \cdot 8 = 512. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So the equation \( z^3 = 512 \text{cis}(3\pi) \) becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ z^3 = 512 \text{cis}(3\pi). \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can express \(\text{cis}(3\pi)\) as \(e^{i(3\pi)}\). Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ z^3 = 512 e^{i(3\pi)}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can simplify \(\text{cis}(3\pi)\) using Euler's formula \( e^{i\theta} = \cos(\theta) + i\sin(\theta) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ e^{i(3\pi)} = \cos(3\pi) + i\sin(3\pi). \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know that \( \cos(3\pi) = -1 \) and \( \sin(3\pi) = 0 \). Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ e^{i(3\pi)} = -1 + i \cdot 0 = -1. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ z^3 = 512 \cdot -1 = -512. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Taking the cube root of both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ z = -\sqrt[3]{512} + i \sqrt[3]{-512} = -8 + i (-8i) = -8 - 8(-1) = -8 + 8 = 0. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the only solution to the equation \( z^3 = -8 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{0}. \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
