[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(30 = 30\), we get 30 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(36 = 36\), we get 36 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(42 = 48\), we get 42 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(54 = 60\), we get 54 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(66 = 72\), we get 66 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(72 = 78\), we get 72 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, we have \(30, 36, 42, 48, 54, 60, 66, 72\) as possible values for \(m\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's check which of these values satisfy \(30 \leq m < 80\) and leave a remainder of 2 when divided by 5:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(30 = 30\), we get 30 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(42 = 72\), we get 42 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for \(66 = 78\), we get 66 as a multiple of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, we have 42 as a possible value for \(m\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, we need to check that 42 leaves a remainder of 2 when divided by 8 and 5:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for 42, we get \(42 \div 8 = 5\) remainder 2.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - for 42, we get \(42 \div 5 = 8\) remainder 2.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Both conditions are satisfied, so the value of \(m\) that satisfies all the conditions is \(\boxed{42}\).<|endoftext|>
