[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \sqrt{2^2 - 2(2) + 2} + \sqrt{-2^2 + 6(2) - 2} = \sqrt{0} + \sqrt{0} = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the smallest real number \(x\) which satisfies the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \(\boxed{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m What is $75\%$ of $40\%$ of $200$? To find \(75\%\) of \(40\%\) of \(200\), we start by expressing the problem in a mathematical form. We need to compute:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0.75 \times 0.40 \times 200
