[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Jeremiah is riding in a car that is traveling 60 miles per hour. At this rate, how many minutes will it take him to travel 20 miles?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many minutes it will take Jeremiah to travel 20 miles at a speed of 60 miles per hour, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Convert the speed from miles per hour to miles per minute:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1 \text{ hour} = 60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore, for every mile traveled in an hour, we need:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{1 \text{ mile}}{60 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{1}{60} \text{ miles per minute}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Calculate the time in minutes to travel 20 miles:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since we need to travel at a speed of 60 miles per hour, we multiply the speed by the time in minutes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Time in minutes} = \frac{20 \text{ miles}}{\frac{1}{60} \text{ miles per minute}} = 20 \times 60 \text{ minutes} = 1200 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Convert the time from minutes to hours:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    To convert the time from minutes to hours, we divide by 60 (since there are 60 minutes in an hour):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Time in hours} = \frac{1200 \text{ minutes}}{60 \text{ minutes per hour}} = 20 \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, it will take Jeremiah \boxed{20} minutes to travel 20 miles.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
