[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m What is the largest prime factor of $1337$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the largest prime factor of \(1337\), we start by finding its prime factorization. Let's go through the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Check for divisibility by small prime numbers:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - \(1337\) is odd, so it is not divisible by \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The sum of the digits of \(1337\) is \(1 + 3 + 3 + 7 = 14\), which is not divisible by \(3\), so \(1337\) is not divisible by \(3\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The last digit of \(1337\) is \(7\), so it is divisible by \(7\). We perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      1337 \div 7 = 191
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      So, \(1337 = 7 \times 191\). Now we need to factorize \(191\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Check for divisibility of \(191\):**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - \(191\) is odd, so it is not divisible by \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The sum of the digits of \(191\) is \(1 + 9 + 1 = 11\), which is not divisible by \(3\), so \(191\) is not divisible by \(3\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - To check for divisibility by \(5\), we look at the last digit of \(191\), which is \(1\). Since \(191\) does not end in \(0\) or \(5\), it is not divisible by \(5\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - To check for divisibility by \(7\), we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      191 \div 7 \approx 27.2857 \quad (\text{not an integer})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      So, \(191\) is not divisible by \(7\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - To check for divisibility by \(11\), we use the alternating sum of the digits \(1 - 9 + 1 = -7\), which is not divisible by \(11\), so \(191\) is not divisible by \(11\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - To check for divisibility by \(13\), we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      191 \div 13 \approx 14.6923 \quad (\text{not an integer})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      So, \(191\) is not divisible by \(13\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - To check for divisibility by \(17\), we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      191 \div 17 \approx 11.9412 \quad (\text{not an integer})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      So, \(191\) is not divisible by \(17\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - To check for divisibility by \(19\), we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      191 \div 19 \approx 10.0538 \quad (\text{not an integer})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      So, \(191\) is not divisible by \(19\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(191\) is not divisible by any prime number less than \(\sqrt{191} \approx 13.83\), the prime factorization of \(191\) is complete.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the prime factorization of \(1337\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1337 = 7^2 \times 191
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The largest prime factor of \(1337\) is \(\boxed{191}\).<|endoftext|>
