[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the number of ways to put 4 indistinguishable balls into 2 indistinguishable boxes, we can use the concept of permutations of a multiset. The formula for the number of ways to distribute \( n \) indistinguishable objects into \( k \) distinguishable bins is given by the multinomial coefficient:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{n!}{n_1! \cdot n_2! \cdot \ldots \cdot n_k!}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \( n = 4 \) (the number of balls) and \( k = 2 \) (the number of boxes). Plugging in these values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{4!}{4! \cdot 2! \cdot 2!}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we calculate the factorials:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4! = 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4! \cdot 2! = 24 \cdot 2 = 48
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2! \cdot 2! = 2 \cdot 2 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we divide the factorial of the total number of balls by the product of the factorials of the boxes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{24}{48} = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the number of ways to distribute 4 indistinguishable balls into 2 indistinguishable boxes is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
