[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ AB + BC = 2 + x + 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 2 + 5 = x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 7 = x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ x = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the length \( CD \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ CD = 5 \text{ units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we need to find the length of \( AC \). Since \( A \) is directly opposite \( D \) and \( C \) is directly opposite \( B \), we can assume \( D \) and \( B \) are directly opposite each other on the line. Therefore:
