[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Cylinder $B$'s height is equal to the radius of cylinder $A$ and cylinder $B$'s radius is equal to the height $h$ of cylinder $A$. If the volume of cylinder $A$ is twice the volume of cylinder $B$, the volume of cylinder $A$ can be written as $N \pi h^3$ cubic units. What is the value of $N$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
