[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      1 & 3 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - For each of these units choices, the remaining two digits automatically determine the tens and hundreds places. For example, if we choose \(1\) for the units place:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \begin{array}{ccc}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      1 & 1 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      1 & 2 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      1 & 3 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Thousands place**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - We now consider the thousands place with 2 choices:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - We can choose any of the 3 digits (1, 2, 3, 4) for the thousands place. For example, we can choose from 3 options:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        \[
