[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - For each of these choices, the remaining 3 digits will automatically determine the hundreds, tens, and units places. For example, if we choose \(4\) for the thousands place:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        \begin{array}{ccc}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        4 & 1 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        4 & 2 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        4 & 3 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m        \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's sum the number of valid combinations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - First digit choices: 3 (2 choices for the units place and 1 choice for the tens place, making 2 choices total).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Second digit choices: Same as the first digit choices.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Third digit choices: Same as the first digit choices.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the total number of distinct three-digit numbers is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
