[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Abigail, Beatrice, and Carson combine their eggs to sell them at the market. If Abigail has 37 eggs, Beatrice has 49 eggs, and Carson has 14 eggs, and if eggs can only be sold in cartons of 12, how many eggs will be left over if all cartons are sold?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many eggs will be left over after selling them all in cartons of 12, we need to first find out the total number of eggs that Abigail, Beatrice, and Carson have combined.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m From the problem, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Abigail has 37 eggs.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Beatrice has 49 eggs.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Carson has 14 eggs.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we calculate the total number of eggs:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 37 + 49 + 14
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Adding these together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 37 + 49 = 86
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 86 + 14 = 100
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the total number of eggs is 100.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we need to determine how many eggs there are when they are all sold in cartons of 12. To do this, we divide the total number of eggs by 12:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 100 \div 12
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Performing the division:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 100 \div 12 = 8 \text{ R } 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This means that 100 divided by 12 gives us a quotient of 8 and a remainder of 4. Therefore, after selling all 100 eggs, there will be:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{4}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, there will be \boxed{4} eggs left over.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
