[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Carlos Montado was born on Saturday, November 9, 2002.  On what day of the week will Carlos be 706 days old? (Spell out the entire day of the week.)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine Carlos Montado's day of the week when he is 706 days old, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Calculate the number of years Carlos has been alive:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \( 706 \div 365 \approx 1.9106 \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since Carlos has been alive for 1 full year and a day (which is 1 day), we need to look at the next year.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Determine the starting year:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We start by finding the remainder when 706 is divided by 365:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    706 \div 365 \approx 1.9106 \implies \text{remainder} = 706 - 1 \times 365 = 401
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So, Carlos has been alive for approximately 1 year (36 weeks) and 401 days.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Find the day of the week for the 1st of the next year:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    To find the day of the week for the 36th day of the next year, we need to find the remainder when 401 days (aLongwhile) is divided by 365. This can be done using modular arithmetic:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    365 \times 401 + \text{result} \equiv 401 \pmod{365}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    First, calculate \( 365 \times 401 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    365 \times 401 = 146455
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Now, find the remainder when 146455 is divided by 365:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    146455 \div 365 \approx 401.807 \implies \text{remainder} = 146455 - 146455 \times 365 + 365 \times 401 = 146455 - 52671050 + 146455 = −52671050 + 146455 = -52524595 \equiv 746 \pmod{365}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    146455 \equiv 746 \pmod{365}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    706 + 746 \equiv 1452 \pmod{365}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Now, we need to find the day of the week immediately after July 4, 2002, which is already known. Let's calculate that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    746 \div 7 \approx 106 \text{ remainder 3} \implies \text{remainder} = 3 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    746 \equiv 3 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 3 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 3 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7} \implies 1452 \equiv 2 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Identify the day of the week:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Carlos is exactly 1452 days after July 4, 2002. Since July has 30 days:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1452 - 4 = 1448 \quad \text{(This is not a full week, so we subtract 1 more month and day)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore, Carlos is 14 days before a full week.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The leap year number is 2002 - 1 = 2001. The day of the week after July 4, 2002 before January 1, 2003, can be found by counting backwards:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    30 - 30 \div 7 \approx 30 - 4 = 26 \implies \text{1452 - 1 month minus 1 day}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The day of the week is 1 day before the beginning of a month, which is Monday. Therefore, Carlos is 1 day before Monday:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \boxed{Wednesday}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
