[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To compute the product of two matrices, we need to multiply the rows of the first matrix by the columns of the second matrix. Let's denote the matrices as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ A = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 5 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ B = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -2 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The product \( C = AB \) is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ C = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 5 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -2 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \cdot 8 + 0 \cdot 1 & 2 \cdot -2 + 0 \cdot 1 \\ 5 \cdot 8 + -3 \cdot 1 & 5 \cdot -2 + -3 \cdot 1 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 2 \cdot 8 + 0 \cdot 1 = 16 + 0 = 16 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 2 \cdot -2 + 0 \cdot 1 = -4 + 0 = -4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 5 \cdot 8 + -3 \cdot 1 = 40 - 3 = 37 \]
