[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Focal Point Function:** The focal point \(\mathbf{P}\) should give us the sum of these vectors as the magnitude of \(\mathbf{P}\). If we denote a point \(P\) on this line in -2D coordinates to lie exactly at the focal point, then \(P\) should be just 10 units away from the origin. Hence, the magnitude of \(\mathbf{P}\) should be 10.
