[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the ordered pair \((j, k)\) that satisfies the equations \(5j - 42k = 1\) and \(2k - j = 3\), we will solve these equations step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we start with the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[2k - j = 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can solve for \(j\) in terms of \(k\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[j = 2k - 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we substitute \(j = 2k - 3\) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[5j - 42k = 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[5(2k - 3) - 42k = 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[10k - 15 - 42k = 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-32k - 15 = 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-32k = 16\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[k = -\frac{16}{32}\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[k = -\frac{1}{2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now that we have \(k = -\frac{1}{2}\), we substitute this value back into the equation \(j = 2k - 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[j = 2\left(-\frac{1}{2}\right) - 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[j = -1 - 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[j = -4\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the ordered pair \((j, k)\) that satisfies both equations is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\left(-4, -\frac{1}{2}\right)\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
