[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To evaluate the expression
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \frac{121 \left( \frac{1}{13} - \frac{1}{17} \right) 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m           + 169 \left( \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{11} \right) + 289 \left( \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13} \right)}{
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m         11 \left( \frac{1}{13} - \frac{1}{17} \right) 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m           + 13 \left( \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{11} \right) + 17 \left( \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13} \right)} \, ,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m we start by simplifying the individual terms of the numerator and the denominator separately.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, simplify the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 121 \left( \frac{1}{13} - \frac{1}{17} \right) + 169 \left( \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{11} \right) + 289 \left( \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 13, 17, 17, and 11 is \(13 \times 13 = 169\). Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 121 \left( \frac{1}{13} - \frac{1}{17} \right) = \frac{121 \times 1}{13 \times 17} - \frac{121 \times 1}{17 \times 17} = \frac{121 \times 17 - 121 \times 13}{169} = \frac{121 \times (17 - 13)}{169} = \frac{121 \times 4}{169} = \frac{484}{169}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 169 \left( \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{11} \right) = \frac{169 \times 11 - 169 \times 17}{169 \times 11} = \frac{169 \times (11 - 17)}{169 \times 11} = \frac{169 \times (-6)}{169 \times 11} = \frac{6 \times 169}{169 \times 11} = \frac{169}{11}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 289 \left( \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13} \right) = \frac{289 \times 13 - 289 \times 1}{289 \times 13} = \frac{289 \times (13 - 1)}{289 \times 13} = \frac{289 \times 12}{289 \times 13} = \frac{12 \times 289}{289 \times 13} = \frac{289}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we substitute these back into the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 484 + \frac{169}{11} + \frac{289}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 11 and 13 is \(143\). Thus, we convert each fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{169}{11} = \frac{169 \times 13}{11 \times 13} = \frac{2197}{143}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{289}{13} = \frac{289 \times 11}{13 \times 11} = \frac{3159}{143}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 484 + \frac{169}{11} + \frac{289}{13} = 484 + \frac{2197}{143} + \frac{3159}{143} = 484 + \frac{5356}{143} = \frac{484 \times 143}{143} + \frac{5356}{143} = \frac{69172}{143} + \frac{5356}{143} = \frac{74528}{143}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we simplify the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 11 \left( \frac{1}{13} - \frac{1}{17} \right) = \frac{11 \times 1}{13 \times 17} - \frac{11 \times 1}{17 \times 17} = \frac{11 \times 17 - 11 \times 13}{221} = \frac{11 \times (17 - 13)}{221} = \frac{11 \times 4}{221} = \frac{44}{221}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 13 \left( \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{11} \right) = \frac{13 \times 1}{13 \times 11} - \frac{13 \times 1}{11 \times 11} = \frac{13 \times (11 - 1)}{13 \times 11} = \frac{13 \times 10}{13 \times 11} = \frac{10}{11}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 17 \left( \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13} \right) = \frac{17 \times 1}{17 \times 13} - \frac{17 \times 1}{13 \times 17} = \frac{17 \times (13 - 1)}{17 \times 13} = \frac{17 \times 12}{17 \times 13} = \frac{12}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the denominator is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{44}{221} + \frac{10}{11} + \frac{12}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 221, 11, and 13 is \(221 \times 11 \times 13 = 37483\). Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{10}{11} = \frac{10 \times 331}{37483} = \frac{331}{37483}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{12}{13} = \frac{12 \times 2651}{37483} = \frac{31822}{37483}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{44}{221} + \frac{10}{11} + \frac{12}{13} = \frac{44 \times 11}{37483} + \frac{331}{37483} + \frac{31822}{37483} = \frac{484 + 331 + 31822}{37483} = \frac{35237}{37483}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Putting it all together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{\frac{74528}{143}}{\frac{35237}{37483}} = \frac{74528}{143} \times \frac{37483}{35237} = \frac{74528 \times 37483}{143 \times 35237} = \frac{2734236296}{47459211} = \frac{15898363}{2492360.5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{15898363}{24923605}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
