[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify the given expression \(\frac{\tan 30^\circ + \tan 40^\circ + \tan 50^\circ + \tan 60^\circ}{\cos 20^\circ}\), we will use trigonometric identities and properties of the tangent function.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, recall the tangent addition formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \tan(A + B) = \frac{\tan A + \tan B}{1 - \tan A \tan B}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can pair the terms in the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \tan 30^\circ + \tan 60^\circ = 1 + \sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \tan 40^\circ + \tan 50^\circ = 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \tan 30^\circ + \tan 40^\circ + \tan 50^\circ + \tan 60^\circ = (1 + \sqrt{3}) + 1 = 2 + \sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to divide this result by \(\cos 20^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{2 + \sqrt{3}}{\cos 20^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we use the identity \(\cos 20^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}\). Substituting this into the expression, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{2 + \sqrt{3}}{\cos 20^\circ} = \frac{2 + \sqrt{3}}{\frac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}} = 2 + \sqrt{3} \cdot \frac{4}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify further, we rationalize the denominator by multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 + \sqrt{3} \cdot \frac{4}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}} = 2 + \sqrt{3} \cdot \frac{4(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})}{6 - 2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 2 + \sqrt{3} \cdot \frac{4(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})}{4} = 2 + \sqrt{3} \cdot (\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 2 + (\sqrt{18} + \sqrt{6}) = 2 + (3\sqrt{2} + \sqrt{6})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the simplified expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{2 + \sqrt{3} + 3\sqrt{2} + \sqrt{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
