[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find all roots of the polynomial \(x^3 + x^2 - 4x - 4\), we need to solve the equation \(x^3 + x^2 - 4x - 4 = 0\). We can use the Rational Root Theorem to determine possible rational roots, and then we will use synthetic division, factoring techniques, or the quadratic formula to find the remaining roots.
