[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to sum the factorials up to \( 100! \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 120 + 3628800 + 1307674368000 \in [120, 5] \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's calculate the last two digits of each number in this sequence:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 120 \Rightarrow 120 \rightarrow 120 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3628800 \Rightarrow 80 \rightarrow 800 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 1307674368000 \Rightarrow 40 \rightarrow 4000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Summing these up:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 120 + 800 + 4000 = 5020 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we need to find the last two digits of each of the last two digits:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 520 \rightarrow 20 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 080 \rightarrow 80 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 0400 \rightarrow 00 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 4000 \rightarrow 00 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Summing these up:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 20 + 80 + 00 + 00 = 100 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the last two digits need to be considered for the final sum, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 5! + 10! + 15! + \cdots + 100! \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The last two digits of each individual factorial are as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 120 \rightarrow 120 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3628800 \rightarrow 800 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 1307674368000 \rightarrow 4000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Summing these up:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 120 + 800 + 4000 = 5020 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the last two digits of the entire sum are:
