[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Eight pounds of feathers and two ounces of gold together cost $\$932$. Fourteen pounds of feathers and three ounces of gold together cost $\$1402$. What is the cost of five pounds of feathers and five ounces of gold?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the problem, we will set up a system of linear equations based on the given information.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's convert all costs to the same unit of currency. We'll use pounds of feathers and ounces of gold as our single unit.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The first equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 8 \text{ pounds of feathers} + 2 \text{ ounces of gold} = 932 \text{ dollars} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The second equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 14 \text{ pounds of feathers} + 3 \text{ ounces of gold} = 1402 \text{ dollars} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can convert the third equation to cents to match the unit of the first equation (dollars):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 14 \text{ pounds} + 3 \text{ ounces of gold} = 1402 \text{ dollars} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's write down the system of equations in standard form:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 8x + 2y = 932 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 14x + 3y = 1402 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We will solve this system using the method of elimination.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we will eliminate one of the variables. To do this, we can make the coefficients of \( x \) in both equations the same (by multiplying the first equation by 7 and the second equation by 16).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Multiply the first equation by 7:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 56x + 14y = 6564 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Multiply the second equation by 16:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 224x + 48y = 22424 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we have the system:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 56x + 14y = 6564 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 224x + 48y = 22424 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we will eliminate \( y \). To do this, we need the coefficients of \( y \) to be the same (or opposite). We can find this by multiplying the first equation by 1.5 (since \( \frac{14}{2} = 7 \) and \( \frac{1}{3} = \frac{1}{3} \)):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 9.6x + 2.25y = 1012.4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we subtract the second equation from this result:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ (9.6x + 2.25y) - (224x + 48y) = 1012.4 - 22424 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 9.6x + 2.25y - 224x - 48y = 1012.4 - 22424 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -214.4x - 25.75y = -21403 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the cost of 5 ounces of feathers and 5 ounces of gold is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{3025} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
