[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To compute \(\tan(-3645^\circ)\), we need to find the equivalent positive angle within the standard range of \([0^\circ, 360^\circ)\) that has the same tangent value. We can use the periodicity of the tangent function, which has a period of \(180^\circ\). This means that \(\tan(-\theta) = -\tan(\theta)\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's simplify the angle byadding \(360^\circ\) until we get an equivalent angle between \(0^\circ\) and \(360^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -3645^\circ + 360 \times 4 = -3645^\circ + 1440^\circ = -2205^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(-2205^\circ\) is still not a multiple of \(360^\circ\), we add another \(360^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -2205^\circ + 360 \times 3 = -2205^\circ + 1080^\circ = -1125^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, \(-1125^\circ\) is still not a multiple of \(360^\circ\), so we add another \(360^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -1125^\circ + 360 \times 3 = -1125^\circ + 1080^\circ = -45^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(-45^\circ\) is still not a multiple of \(360^\circ\), we continue:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -45^\circ + 360 \times 2 = -45^\circ + 720^\circ = 675^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, \(-675^\circ\) is within the standard range of \(0^\circ\) to \(360^\circ\). We can now find \(\tan(675^\circ)\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \tan(675^\circ) = \tan(540^\circ + 30^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know that \(\tan(45^\circ) = 1\). Specifically, \(\tan(540^\circ + 30^\circ) = \tan(30^\circ)\) because:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \tan(540^\circ + 30^\circ) = \tan(30^\circ) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m And \(\tan(30^\circ) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the value of \(\tan(-3645^\circ)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
