[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Check divisibility by 7:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    122 \div 7 = 17 \quad (\text{an integer, so 7 is a factor})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Now, we can divide 122 by 7 to find other factors that include 7.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    122 \div 7 = 17
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. **Check if 17 is a prime number:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    17 \text{ is a prime number}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. **Sum of the prime factors:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    7 + 7 + 17 = 31
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the sum of the distinct prime factors of 735 is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{31}
