[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the modulo 4 residue of \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Find the residues of each number modulo 4:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - \(121 \mod 4\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      121 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 1 \implies 121 \equiv 1 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - \(122 \mod 4\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      122 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 2 \implies 122 \equiv 2 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - \(123 \mod 4\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      123 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 3 \implies 123 \equiv 3 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Multiply the residues:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123) \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Substitute the residues:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3) \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Calculate the product:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1 \cdot 2 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2 \cdot 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Find the remainder when 6 is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    6 \mod 4 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Multiply the result by 417 and take the modulo 4 again:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Multiply 2 by 417:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2 \cdot 417 = 834
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Find the remainder when 834 is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    834 \div 4 = 208 \text{ remainder } 0 \implies 834 \equiv 0 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the modulo 4 residue of \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123\) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
