[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's expand the expression \((x-3)(x-2)\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x-3)(x-2) = x^2 - 2x - 3x + 6 = x^2 - 5x + 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, substitute this expansion back into the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x^2 - 5x + 7) - (x^2 - 5x + 6).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, distribute the \(-1\) through the second set of parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x^2 - 5x + 7) - (x^2 - 5x + 6) = x^2 - 5x + 7 - x^2 + 5x - 6.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x^2 - x^2) + (-5x + 5x) + (7 - 6) = 0 + 0 + 1 = 1.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the simplified expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{1}.
