[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Golf balls are packaged by stacking three balls vertically in a box. Given that the height of the box is 13.5 cm, and that the golf balls are touching each other and the ends of the box, what is the number of centimeters in the circumference of each golf ball? Express your answer as a common fraction in terms of $\pi$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Note: To measure the circumference, take the largest circle on the surface of the golf ball.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the circumference of each golf ball, we need to understand the geometry involved. When three golf balls are stacked vertically in a box, they form a square of side length equal to the distance between the centers of any two adjacent balls. This side length is the same as the height of the box divided by 4 (since there are two balls on either side of the center ball).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given that the height of the box is 13.5 cm, the distance between the centers of two adjacent balls is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{13.5}{4} = 3.375 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The circumference of a circle is given by the formula \(C = 2\pi r\), where \(r\) is the radius of the circle (or in this case, the distance between the centers of two adjacent balls). Therefore, the circumference of each golf ball is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2\pi \times 3.375 = 6.75\pi \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the number of centimeters in the circumference of each golf ball is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{6.75\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{9\pi}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
