[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given the function {eq}G(x) = \int \limits_1^\frac{1}{2} xe^{\frac{b}{x}} dx {/eq}, where {eq}b > 0 {/eq} is a constant, find the derivative {eq}G'(x) {/eq}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the derivative \( G'(x) \) of the function \( G(x) = \int_1^\frac{1}{2} e^{\frac{b}{x}} \, dx \), we will use the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, which states that if \( F(x) = \int_f^g h(x) \, dx \), then \( F'(x) = h(g) \cdot g'(x) - h(f) \cdot f'(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In our case, \( f(x) = 1 \), \( g(x) = \frac{1}{2} \), \( F(x) = e^{\frac{b}{x}} \), and \( h(t) = e^t \). Applying the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ G'(x) = e^{\frac{1}{2}} \cdot \frac{d}{dx} \left( e^{\frac{b}{x}} \right) - e^{\frac{1}{2}} \cdot 1. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we calculate the derivative inside the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \frac{d}{dx} \left( e^{\frac{b}{x}} \right) = e^{\frac{b}{x}} \cdot \frac{d}{dx} \left( \frac{b}{x} \right) = e^{\frac{b}{x}} \cdot \left( -\frac{b}{x^2} \right) = -\frac{b}{x^2} e^{\frac{b}{x}}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, substituting this back into the expression for \( G'(x) \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ G'(x) = e^{\frac{1}{2}} \left( -\frac{b}{x^2} e^{\frac{b}{x}} \right) - e^{\frac{1}{2}} = -e^{\frac{1}{2}} \cdot \frac{b}{x^2} e^{\frac{b}{x}} - e^{\frac{1}{2}}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combining the terms involving \( e^{\frac{1}{2}} \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ G'(x) = -e^{\frac{1}{2}} \frac{b}{x^2} e^{\frac{b}{x}} - e^{\frac{1}{2}} = e^{\frac{1}{2}} \left( -\frac{b}{x^2} e^{\frac{b}{x}} - 1 \right). \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the derivative \( G'(x) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{e^{\frac{1}{2}} \left( -\frac{b}{x^2} e^{\frac{b}{x}} - 1 \right)}. \]
