[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the value of \(6 \# 2\), we use the definition of the operation \(\#\) which is defined as \(a \# b = a + \frac{a}{b}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, substitute \(a = 6\) and \(b = 2\) into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 \# 2 = 6 + \frac{6}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, simplify \(\frac{6}{2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{6}{2} = 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 \# 2 = 6 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, add 6 and 3:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 + 3 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the value of \(6 \# 2\) is \(\boxed{9}\).<|endoftext|>
