[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let $\mathbf{v}_1,$ $\mathbf{v}_2,$ $\dots,$ $\mathbf{v}_k$ be unit vectors such that
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\mathbf{v}_1 + \mathbf{v}_2 + \dots + \mathbf{v}_k = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}.\]Find the smallest possible value of $k.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Note: A unit vector is a vector of magnitude 1.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the smallest possible value of \( k \) such that \(\mathbf{v}_1 + \mathbf{v}_2 + \dots + \mathbf{v}_k = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to minimize the volume of the parallelepiped formed by \(\mathbf{v}_1, \mathbf{v}_2, \dots, \mathbf{v}_k\). The volume of a parallelepiped formed by vectors \(\mathbf{v}_1, \mathbf{v}_2, \dots, \mathbf{v}_k\) is given by the absolute value of the determinant of the matrix whose columns are these vectors. That is,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Volume} = \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{v}_1 & \mathbf{v}_2 & \dots & \mathbf{v}_k
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right| = \left| \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 & 5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 & 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This determinant can be simplified using the formula for the determinant of a doubly indexed matrix. The matrix can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 & 5 & \cdots & 0 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & -5 & \cdots & 0 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 & 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 6 P - 5 Q
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \(P = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 & 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix}\) and \(Q = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 & -5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix}\). The matrix \(P\) and \(Q\) are permutations of each other, so \(P Q = P\). Therefore, the volume is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left| \det(6P - 5Q) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To minimize the volume, we need to find \(P\) and \(Q\) such that the volume is minimized. We start by considering the vectors \(\mathbf{v}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{v}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}\). A orthogonal basis for \(\mathbb{R}^2\) is \(\{\mathbf{v}_1, \mathbf{v}_2\}\), and their sum is \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\), which is the direction of our vectors.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we form the matrices \(Q\) and \(P\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Q = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 & -5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix}, \quad P = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & 1 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -1 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The volume of the parallelepiped is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left| \det(6P - 5Q) \right| = \left| \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 & 5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix} \right|,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left| 6 \det P - 5 \det Q \right| = \left| 6 \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & -5 & 0 & \cdots & 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix} \right| = 6 \left| \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & -5 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix} \right|,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where the second determinant runs over a \(5 \times 5\) block. This determinant is symmetric and can be computed as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & -5 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{pmatrix} = 6^{-5} \cdot 5^5 \cdot 1^4 = 6^{-5} \cdot 625 = 15625/6^5 = 15625/7776 = \frac{25}{108} = \frac{25}{108}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the smallest possible value of \(k\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m k = 3.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
