[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d$ be positive integers such that
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix}.\]Find the smallest possible value of $a + b + c + d.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the given matrix equation, we start with the product of the matrices:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Calculating the right-hand side of the initial equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 18a - 20b & 12a - 13b \\ 18c - 20d & 12c - 13d \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The left-hand side of the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3a & 3b \\ 3c & 3d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Equating the elements, we get the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. \( a = 18a - 20b \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. \( b = 12a - 13b \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. \( c = 18c - 20d \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. \( d = 12c - 13d \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's solve these equations step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **First equation: \( a = 18a - 20b \)**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ a - 18a = -20b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -17a = -20b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 17a = 20b \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ b = \frac{17a}{20} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Second equation: \( b = 12a - 13b \)**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ b + 13b = 12a \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 14b = 12a \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ b = \frac{6a}{7} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Third equation: \( c = 18c - 20d \)**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ c - 20c = -20d \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -19c = -20d \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ c = \frac{20d}{19} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Fourth equation: \( d = 12c - 13d \)**
