[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Multiply the numbers starting from the rightmost digits:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Multiply \(4\) by \(6\), which is \(24\). Write down \(0\) and carry over \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Multiply \(4\) by \(6\) and add the carry-over \(2\), which is \(24 + 2 = 26\). Write down \(26\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Next, move to the leftmost digits and multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Multiply \(3\) by \(6\), which is \(18\). Write down \(2\) and \(18\) carry over \(18\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Multiply \(3\) by \(6\) and add the carry-over \(18\), which is \(30 + 18 = 48\). Write down \(48\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Putting it all together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{r}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   0.4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \cdot 0.6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \hline
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   0.24 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   + 26 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the result of \(0.4 \cdot 0.6\) is \(\boxed{0.24}\).<|endoftext|>
