[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \(\det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B})\), we will use the properties of determinants, specifically the scalar multiplication property. The scalar multiplication property states that for any matrices \(\mathbf{A}\), \(\mathbf{B}\), and \(\mathbf{C}\), and real numbers \(k\) and \(\lambda\),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \lambda \det (\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = \det (\mathbf{O}) \cdot \lambda = \lambda^2, \quad k \lambda \det (\mathbf{C}) = \det (\mathbf{O}) \cdot k \lambda = \det (\mathbf{O})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In this problem, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \det (\mathbf{A}) = -1 \quad \text{and} \quad \det (\mathbf{B}) = 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \(\det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B})\), we can use the property of determinants with scalar multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3 \det (\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = \det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we compute \(3 \det (\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B})\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3 \det (\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = 3 \cdot (-1) = -3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we use the scalar multiplication property:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = \det (\mathbf{O}) \cdot (-3) = -3 \det (\mathbf{O})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(\det (\mathbf{O}) = 1\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = -3 \cdot 1 = -3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the determinant of \(3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
