[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m How many feet long is the shadow of a 20-foot flagpole if a 6-foot woman standing at the base of the flagpole has a shadow that is nine feet long?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the length of the shadow of the 20-foot flagpole, we can use trigonometry. The shadow formed by the flagpole is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where the shadow is the opposite side, and the height of the man is the adjacent side. The woman's height is 6 feet, and the distance from the base of the flagpole to the point where the woman's shadow starts is the adjacent side of a right triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we need to find the ratio of the woman's height to the man's height:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Ratio} = \frac{\text{Height of man}}{\text{Height of woman}} = \frac{6 \text{ feet}}{6 \text{ feet}} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This means the shadow of the man will be the same size as the man himself, regardless of his height. Therefore, we can use the Proportion of the triangles formed by the man, the shadow of the man, the flagpole, and its shadow.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In the right triangle, the length of the shadow of the man is the adjacent side to the angle whose tangent is the ratio of the length of the man's shadow to the length of the shadow of the man. So, the length of the shadow of the man is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Shadow of man} = \text{adjacent} \times \text{angle} = 6 \text{ feet} \times 1 = 6 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the length of the shadow of the 20-foot flagpole is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{6}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
