[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \( g(0) \) for the function \( g(x) = 3x - 4 \), we need to substitute \( x = 0 \) into the function. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Start with the function:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    g(x) = 3x - 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Substitute \( x = 0 \) into the function:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    g(0) = 3(0) - 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    3(0) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    g(0) = 0 - 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Perform the subtraction:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    0 - 4 = -4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( g(0) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-4}
