[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We flip a fair coin 10 times.  What is the probability that we get heads in exactly 8 of the 10 flips?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the probability that we get heads in exactly 8 out of 10 flips of a fair coin, we need to use the binomial probability formula. The binomial probability formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( n \) is the number of trials (in this case, 10 flips),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( k \) is the number of successful trials (in this case, 8 heads),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( p \) is the probability of success on a single trial (in this case, 0.5 for heads),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\) is the binomial coefficient.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we calculate the binomial coefficient \(\binom{10}{8}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \binom{10}{8} = \frac{10!}{8!2!} = \frac{10 \times 9}{2 \times 1} = 45
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we calculate \( p^k \) and \( (1-p)^{n-k} \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m p^k = 0.5^8 = \frac{1}{256}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (1-p)^{n-k} = 0.5^{10-8} = 0.5^2 = 0.25
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we substitute these values into the binomial probability formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m P(X = 8) = 45 \times \left(\frac{1}{256}\right) \times 0.25
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m P(X = 8) = 45 \times \frac{0.25}{256} = \frac{45 \times 0.25}{256} = \frac{11.25}{256} = 0.044209375
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the probability that we get heads in exactly 8 out of 10 flips is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{0.044209375}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \dfrac{45}{1024}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
