[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many feet of the statue each inch of the model represents, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Convert the height of the statue to feet:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The height of the statue is given in feet. Let's assume the height of the statue is \( h \) feet. Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    h = 60 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Determine the scale factor:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The scale model has a height of 4 inches. To find the scale factor, we divide the height of the scale model by the height of the original statue:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Scale factor} = \frac{4 \text{ inches}}{60 \text{ feet}} = \frac{1 \text{ inch}}{15 \text{ feet}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Calculate the height of one inch of the model:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    To find out how many feet each inch of the model represents, we multiply the height of one inch of the model by the scale factor:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Height of one inch in the model} = h \times \frac{1 \text{ inch}}{15 \text{ feet}} = 60 \times \frac{1 \text{ inch}}{15 \text{ feet}} = 4 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, each inch of the model represents \boxed{4} inches.<|endoftext|>
