[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the remainder when the sum \(1 + 12 + 123 + 1234 + 12345 + 123456 + 1234567 + 12345678\) is divided by 5, we can use modular arithmetic. Specifically, we can simplify the problem by finding the sum modulo 5 and then finding the remainder of each number modulo 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Simplify the sum:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1 + 12 + 123 + 1234 + 12345 + 123456 + 1234567 + 12345678 \equiv 0 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    This is because the sum of the sequence is divisible by 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Break down each number modulo 5:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    12 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    123 \equiv 3 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1234 \equiv 4 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    12345 \equiv 0 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    123456 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1234567 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    12345678 \equiv 6 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Add the numbers modulo 5:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (1 + 12 + 123 + 1234 + 12345 + 123456 + 1234567 + 12345678) \equiv 0 + 5 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    0 + 5 = 5 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So, the remainder when the sum is divided by 5 is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{0}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
