[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Find the complement of the 42-degree angle.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The complement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 90 degrees. So, we calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Complement} = 90^\circ - 42^\circ = 48^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Determine the supplement of the complement.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The supplement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 180 degrees. So, we calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Supplement} = 180^\circ - 48^\circ = 132^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \(\boxed{132}\).<|endoftext|>
