[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the measure of the largest angle in an isosceles triangle where one of the angles opposite an equal side is \(40^\circ\), we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the given information:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - We have an isosceles triangle with one angle equal to \(40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The second angle opposite the equal side is also \(40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Therefore, the third angle is also \(40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Understand the properties of an isosceles triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - An isosceles triangle has two equal angles.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \(180^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Sum of angles in a triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Let the angles of the triangle be \(x\), \(x\), and \(40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - According to the angle sum property of a triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      x + x + 40^\circ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Simplify the equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2x + 40^\circ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. **Solve for \(x\):**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2x = 180^\circ - 40^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2x = 140^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    x = 70^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. **Identify the largest angle:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The angles opposite the equal sides (which are both \(40^\circ\)) are both \(40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Therefore, the largest angle in the triangle is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \boxed{70}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]<|endoftext|>
