[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The $24^\text{th}$ day of a particular month is a Saturday. On what day of the week was the first day of that month?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the weekday on the $24^\text{th}$ day of a month when $24$ days are equal to $6$ Saturdays, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Calculate the number of weekdays in 6 Saturdays:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Since there are 7 days in a week, the number of所需的天数是:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      6 \times 7 = 42
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Determine the total number of days to go into including 42 total days:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - If 40 days - 1 day (Saturday) equals 40 days - 1 = 39 days. So, we need to add:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      42 - 39 = 3 \text{ additional day(s)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Identify the weekday corresponding to 3 additional days:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - There are 7 days in a week, so 3 additional days anywhere follows 3 days. The weekdays are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Monday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Tuesday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Wednesday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Thursday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Friday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Saturday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Sunday
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Since we need exactly 3 days and we know that Saturday starts at the $24^\text{th}$, we look at the corresponding days:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - From Weekday 1 to Weekday 6, there are only 5 days (including Saturday). Therefore, any weekday that comes after Saturday one day before the $24^\text{th}$ day will not be a Saturday.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Conclude the weekday on the $24^\text{th}$ day:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The only weekdays that include a Saturday are the days immediately after Saturday:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      - Since 24 days make up 24 complete weeks, the $24^\text{th}$ day falls in Weekday 4 of the next week, starting from Weekday 5 (Saturday).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Hence, the first day of the month was \boxed{Thursday}.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
