[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3 \cdot 3^t + \sqrt{9 \cdot 9^t} = 18 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3 \cdot 3^t + \sqrt{9^1 \cdot 9^t} = 18 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3 \cdot 3^t + 9 \cdot 3^t = 18 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3 \cdot 3^t + 9 \cdot 3^t = 18 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 12 \cdot 3^t = 18 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, solve for \( 3^t \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 12 \cdot 3^t = 18 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3^t = \frac{18}{12} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3^t = \frac{3}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To isolate \( t \), we recognize that \( 3^t = \frac{3}{2} \) can be rewritten using the natural logarithm:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3^t \ln 3 = \ln \left( \frac{3}{2} \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ t \ln 3 = \ln \left( \frac{3}{2} \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ t = \frac{\ln \left( \frac{3}{2} \right)}{\ln 3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the solution to the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{\frac{\ln \left( \frac{3}{2} \right)}{\ln 3}} \]<|endoftext|>
