[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Certainly! Let's break down the problem step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Understand the scaling relationship:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The scale ratio is the ratio of the height of the actual statue to the height of the model.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Scale ratio} = \frac{\text{Height of actual statue}}{\text{Height of model}} = \frac{60 \text{ feet}}{4 \text{ inches}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Perform the division:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Scale ratio} = \frac{60}{4} = 15
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Conclusion:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    One inch of the model represents 15 feet of the actual height of the statue.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, one inch of the model represents \boxed{15} feet of the actual statue.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
