[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let $z_1, z_2, z_3, \dots, z_{12}$ be the 12 zeroes of the polynomial $z^{12} - 2^{36}$. For each $j$, let $w_j$ be one of $z_j$ or $iz_j$. In other words, different values of $w_j$ correspond to different zeroes $z_j$ of the polynomial. For example, if $z_1 = \sqrt{2} + i\sqrt{2}$, then we could choose $-z_1 = -(\sqrt{2} + i\sqrt{2}) = -\sqrt{2} - i\sqrt{2}$ or $i z_1 = i(\sqrt{2} + i\sqrt{2}) = i\sqrt{2} - i^2\sqrt{2} = -\sqrt{2} + i\sqrt{2}$, and these two values of $w_j$ correspond to different zeroes $z_j$ of the polynomial.
