[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the problem, we first need to identify the 12 zeros of the polynomial \(z^{12} - 2^{36}\). The zeros are the 12th roots of \(2^{36} = 2^9 \cdot 2^6 = 512 \cdot 64 = 32768\). These roots are given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[z_k = 2^{36/12} \cdot e^{2k\pi i / 12} = 2^3 \cdot e^{2k\pi i / 12} = 8 \cdot e^{2k\pi i / 12} = 8e^{k\pi i / 6}, \quad k = 0, 1, \ldots, 11.\]
