[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We start by checking divisibility by smaller prime numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Divisibility by 2:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \( 9951 \) is odd, so it is not divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Divisibility by 3:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits of \( 9951 \) is \( 9 + 9 + 5 + 1 = 24 \), which is divisible by 3. Therefore, \( 9951 \) is divisible by 3.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    9951 \div 3 = 3317
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
