[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      Since 301 is an integer, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      3317 = 11 \times 301
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      So, the prime factorization of 3317 is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      3317 = 3 \times 11^2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. **Combining the factorizations:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The prime factorization of \( 9951 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
