[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To convert the decimal number \(115_{10}\) to base 11, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 11 and keep track of the remainders. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Divide 115 by 11:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    115 \div 11 = 10 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 15
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So, the least significant digit (rightmost) in base 11 is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Divide the quotient 10 by 11:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    10 \div 11 = 0 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 10
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The next digit in base 11 is 0, and we start over because the division by 11 is no longer possible after 10 (since the remainder is 10).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the base 11 representation of \(115_{10}\) is obtained by listing the remainders from most significant to least significant:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 105_{11}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
