[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Triangle $ABC$ has sides of length 5, 12 and 13 units, and triangle $DEF$ has sides of length 8, 15 and 17 units. What is the ratio of the area of triangle $ABC$ to the area of triangle $DEF$? Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the ratio of the areas of triangles \(ABC\) and \(DEF\), we first need to calculate the areas using the given side lengths. The area of a triangle that can be inscribed in a right triangle with legs of lengths \(a\) and \(b\) and hypotenuse \(c\) can be found using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times a \times b
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For triangle \(ABC\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The hypotenuse \(c = 13\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - One leg \(a = 5\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The other leg \(b = 12\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the area of triangle \(ABC\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area}_{ABC} = \frac{1}{2} \times 5 \times 12 = \frac{1}{2} \times 60 = 30 \text{ square units}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For triangle \(DEF\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The hypotenuse \(c = 17\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - One leg \(a = 8\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The other leg \(b = 15\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the area of triangle \(DEF\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area}_{DEF} = \frac{1}{2} \times 8 \times 15 = \frac{1}{2} \times 120 = 60 \text{ square units}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, the ratio of the area of triangle \(ABC\) to the area of triangle \(DEF\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Ratio} = \frac{\text{Area}_{ABC}}{\text{Area}_{DEF}} = \frac{30}{60} = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the ratio of the area of triangle \(ABC\) to the area of triangle \(DEF\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
