[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let $\mathbf{v}$ be a vector such that
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\left\| \mathbf{v} + \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \right\| = 8.\]Find the smallest possible value of $\|\mathbf{v}\|.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the smallest possible value of \(\|\mathbf{v}\|\), we start with the given equation for the vector \(\mathbf{v}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left\| \mathbf{v} + \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \right\| = 8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This can be rewritten using the dot product as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \|\mathbf{v}\| + \left\| \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \right\| = 8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\) has a norm \(\sqrt{3^2 + (-1)^2} = \sqrt{9 + 1} = \sqrt{10}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \|\mathbf{v}\| + \sqrt{10} = 8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \(\|\mathbf{v}\|\), we isolate \(\|\mathbf{v}\|\) on one side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \|\mathbf{v}\| = 8 - \sqrt{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The smallest possible value of \(\|\mathbf{v}\|\) is when \(\|\mathbf{v}\| = 0\), which occurs when \(\mathbf{v}\) is a vector that satisfies the given norm condition. In this case, \(\|\mathbf{v}\| = 0\), and \(\left\| \mathbf{v} + \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \right\| = 8\) is satisfied because \(0 + \sqrt{10} = 8\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the smallest possible value of \(\|\mathbf{v}\|\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{0}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 8 - \sqrt{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
