[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Understand the expected value \(E[u]\) in the context of the performance of the game:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The problem states that if the dart lands at \(u\), then \(A \cdot u = \frac{210}{49} + \frac{9}{49} \cdot u^2\). This expression can be matched with the expected value \(E[u]\) if \(u\) is chosen such that \(A\) is such that the proportion of accurate throws is \(E[u]\). Assuming the expected value \(E[u]\) is correctly specified, the performance of the game will be influenced by the chosen value of \(u\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
