[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine in which quarter of the circle Joneal stopped, we first need to calculate the distance Joneal runs on the track and determine where this distance falls on the circumference of the circular track.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Calculate the total distance Joneal runs:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Total distance} = \text{Circumference} = 50 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Convert the distance from feet to miles:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1 \text{ mile} = 5280 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Distance in miles} = \frac{50 \text{ feet}}{5280 \text{ feet/mile}} = \frac{50}{5280} = \frac{5}{528} \text{ miles} \approx 0.009524 \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Determine the position of Joneal’s running?**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since Joneal runs one mile, he will complete half of the track. If we assume the track is 50 feet in length, half of 50 feet is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Half track length} = \frac{50 \text{ feet}}{2} = 25 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Find the position of Joneal on the track:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Joneal runs from point \( S \) to point \( A \), which is 25 feet from the starting point. On the track, 25 feet corresponds to 25 points from the starting point (since each point is 1 inch).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. **Determine the quarter of the circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since Joneal runs 12 points from the starting point, he will stop at point \( A \sim 60^\circ \) of the quarter circle (which is next to the \( B \) point).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the quarter of the circle where Joneal stopped is \(\boxed{B}\).<|endoftext|>
