[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To compute \(\tan 135^\circ\), we will use the properties of the tangent function and trigonometric identities. Let's go through the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the reference angle:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The angle \(135^\circ\) is in the second quadrant. The reference angle for \(135^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    180^\circ - 135^\circ = 45^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Determine the tangent of the reference angle:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The tangent of the reference angle \(45^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \tan 45^\circ = 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Use the tangent identity for the quadrants:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    In the second quadrant, the tangent of an angle is negative. Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \tan 135^\circ = -\tan 45^\circ = -1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the value of \(\tan 135^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
