[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to find the real roots of this polynomial. We can use the Rational Root Theorem to test possible rational roots. The possible rational roots are the factors of the constant term (18) divided by the factors of the leading coefficient (1), which are \(\pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 3, \pm 6, \pm 9, \pm 18\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's test \(x = 2\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2^3 - 9(2)^2 + 14(2) + 18 = 8 - 36 + 28 + 18 = 10 \neq 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So \(x = 2\) is not a root. Let's test \(x = 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^3 - 9(3)^2 + 14(3) + 18 = 27 - 81 + 42 + 18 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So \(x = 3\) is a root. We can use synthetic division to factor \(x - 3\) out of \(x^3 - 9x^2 + 14x + 18\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{r|rrrr}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3 & 1 & -9 & 14 & 18 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   &   & 3 & -36 & -48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   & 1 & -6 & -22 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The quotient is \(x^2 - 6x - 6\), so:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x^3 - 9x^2 + 14x + 18 = (x - 3)(x^2 - 6x - 6).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we need to solve the quadratic equation \(x^2 - 6x - 6 = 0\) using the quadratic formula \(x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \frac{6 \pm \sqrt{36 + 24}}{2} = \frac{6 \pm \sqrt{60}}{2} = \frac{6 \pm 2\sqrt{15}}{2} = 3 \pm \sqrt{15}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So the solutions to the original equation are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = 3 + \sqrt{15}, \quad x = 3 - \sqrt{15}, \quad x = 2.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Putting it all together, the real solutions are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
