[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many boys didn't bring their calculators to class, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of students who brought their calculators to class.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Determine the number of girls who brought their calculators to class.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Find out how many boys did not bring their calculators to class.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's calculate the total number of students who brought their calculators to class. We know:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - 16 boys
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - 22 students in total
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - 13 girls
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The total number of students who brought calculators is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 16 \text{ (boys)} + 22 \text{ (students)} - 13 \text{ (girls)} = 15 \text{ students} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we know that 13 of these 15 students are girls. Therefore, the number of boys who brought calculators is:
