[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many inches taller Yao Ming was than Earl Boykins in 2003, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Convert the heights of Yao Ming and Earl Boykins from feet and inches to centimeters.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Calculate the difference in height.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Step 1: Convert heights to centimeters.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - **Yao Ming's height in centimeters:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   7'5'' \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} \times 2.54 \text{ cm/inch}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   First, convert \(7\) feet to inches:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   7 \text{ feet} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} = 84 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   Then, convert \(5\) inches to inches:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   5 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   Now, add these to the feet and convert:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   84 \text{ inches} + 5 \text{ inches} = 89 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   Finally, multiply by 12 inches per foot and 2.54 cm per inch:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   89 \text{ inches} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} \times 2.54 \text{ cm/inch} = 2088.48 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   So, Yao Ming's height in centimeters is 2088.48 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - **Earl Boykins' height in centimeters:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   5'5'' \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} \times 2.54 \text{ cm/inch}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   First, convert \(5\) feet to inches:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   5 \text{ feet} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} = 60 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   Then, convert \(5\) inches to inches:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   5 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   Now, add these to the feet and convert:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   60 \text{ inches} + 5 \text{ inches} = 65 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   Finally, multiply by 12 inches per foot and 2.54 cm per inch:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   65 \text{ inches} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} \times 2.54 \text{ cm/inch} = 1925.2 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m   So, Earl Boykins' height in centimeters is 1925.2 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m **Step 2: Calculate the difference in height.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Difference} = 2088.48 \text{ cm} - 1925.2 \text{ cm} = 163.28 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, Yao Ming was \boxed{163.28} inches taller than Earl Boykins in 2003.<|endoftext|>
