[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the number of ways four people can sit in a row of five chairs, we can consider this as a permutation problem where we are arranging four people in five seats.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The first person can be seated in any of the 5 positions. After the first person is seated, the second person can be seated in any of the remaining 4 positions. This pattern continues until the last person, who can be seated in any of the remaining 1 position.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the total number of ways to arrange four people in a row of five chairs is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 120 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the number of ways four people can sit in a row of five chairs is \(\boxed{120}\).<|endoftext|>
