[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ 13 & -2 \end{pmatrix},\]compute $(\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{-1}.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \((\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{-1}\) for the given matrix \(\mathbf{A}\), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Compute \(\mathbf{A}^{-1}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The matrix \(\mathbf{A}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ 13 & -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The formula for the inverse of a 2x2 matrix \(\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \mathbf{A}^{-1} = \frac{1}{ad - bc} \begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\ -c & a \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    For \(\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ 13 & -2 \end{pmatrix}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    a = 2, \quad b = 7, \quad c = 13, \quad d = -2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Calculate the determinant of \(\mathbf{A}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \det(\mathbf{A}) = ad - bc = (2)(-2) - (7)(13) = -4 - 91 = -95
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Now, compute \(\mathbf{A}^{-1}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \mathbf{A}^{-1} = \frac{1}{-95} \begin{pmatrix} -2 & -7 \\ -13 & 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{-2}{-95} & \frac{-7}{-95} \\ \frac{-13}{-95} & \frac{2}{-95} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{2}{95} & \frac{7}{95} \\ \frac{13}{95} & -\frac{2}{95} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Compute \((\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{-1}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The inverse of \(\mathbf{A}^{-1}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{-1} = \frac{1}{\text{det}(\mathbf{A}^{-1})} \mathbf{A}^{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    First, calculate \(\text{det}(\mathbf{A}^{-1})\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{det}(\mathbf{A}^{-1}) = \det\left(\begin{pmatrix} \frac{2}{95} & \frac{7}{95} \\ \frac{13}{95} & -\frac{2}{95} \end{pmatrix}\right) = \left(\frac{2}{95} \right) \left(-\frac{2}{95}\right) - \left(\frac{7}{95}\right) \left(\frac{13}{95}\right) = -\frac{4}{9025} - \frac{91}{9025} = -\frac{95}{9025} = -\frac{19}{1805}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{-1} = \frac{1}{-\frac{19}{1805}} \begin{pmatrix} \frac{2}{95} & \frac{7}{95} \\ \frac{13}{95} & -\frac{2}{95} \end{pmatrix} = -\frac{1805}{19} \begin{pmatrix} \frac{2}{95} & \frac{7}{95} \\ \frac{13}{95} & -\frac{2}{95} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Multiply each element by \(-\frac{1805}{19}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    (\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{1805}{19} \cdot \frac{2}{95} & -\frac{1805}{19} \cdot \frac{7}{95} \\ -\frac{1805}{19} \cdot \frac{13}{95} & -\frac{1805}{19} \cdot -\frac{2}{95} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{1805 \cdot 2}{19 \cdot 95} & -\frac{1805 \cdot 7}{19 \cdot 95} \\ -\frac{1805 \cdot 13}{19 \cdot 95} & \frac{1805 \cdot 2}{19 \cdot 95} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Simplify each element:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{1805 \cdot 2}{19 \cdot 95} = \frac{3610}{1805} = \frac{692}{361}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    -\frac{1805 \cdot 7}{19 \cdot 95} = -\frac{12635}{1805} = -\frac{2527}{361}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{1805 \cdot 13}{19 \cdot 95} = \frac{23565}{1805} = \frac{4315}{361}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{1805 \cdot 2}{19 \cdot 95} = \frac{3610}{1805} = \frac{692}{361}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Thus, the inverse of \(\mathbf{A}^{-1}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -\frac{692}{361} & -\frac{2527}{361} \\ -\frac{4315}{361} & \frac{692}{361} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ 13 & -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
