[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the division $0.18\div0.003$, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Division in Scientific Notation**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    For the division of $0.18\div0.003$, we can directly perform the division by moving the decimal point in both numbers to the right by the same number of places.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    In this case, we start with $0.18$ and divide it by $0.003$ by adjusting the decimal places:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    0.18 \div 0.003
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Moving the decimal point 3 places to the right in $0.18$ gives us $180$, and moving it 3 places to the left in $0.003$ gives us $3$:
