[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Rearrange the equation to match the standard form \((y - k)^2 = -4p(x - h)\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    y^2 = -12x
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Now, we can see that this equation is in the form \((y - k)^2 = -4p(x - h)\), where \((h, k) = (0, 0)\) and \(4p = -12\). Solving for \(p\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
