[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the integer \( n \) that satisfies \( 0 \leq n < 19 \) and \( -200 \equiv n \pmod{19} \), we need to find the number \( n \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ n = 19k - 200 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \( k \) is an integer and \( 0 \leq n < 19 \). This means:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 19k - 200 \geq 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 19k \geq 200 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ k \geq \frac{200}{19} \approx 10.5263 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \( k \) must be an integer, the smallest value for \( k \) is 11. We can now find the corresponding value of \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ n = 19 \cdot 11 - 200 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ n = 209 - 200 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ n = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the integer \( n \) that satisfies the conditions is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{9} \]<|endoftext|>
