[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The points $A = (3,-4,2),$ $B = (5,-8,5),$ $C = (4,-3,0),$ and $D = (6,-7,3)$ in space form a flat quadrilateral.  Find the area of this quadrilateral.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the area of the quadrilateral formed by the points \( A = (3, -4, 2) \), \( B = (5, -8, 5) \), \( C = (4, -3, 0) \), and \( D = (6, -7, 3) \) in three-dimensional space, we can use the Gauss-Markoff formula. The formula for the area of a quadrilateral in 3D coordinates is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left\| \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} \right\|
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we need to find the vectors \(\vec{AB}\), \(\vec{AC}\), and \(\vec{AD}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{AB} = B - A = (5 - 3, -8 - (-4), 5 - 2) = (2, -4, 3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{AC} = C - A = (4 - 3, -3 - (-4), 0 - 2) = (1, 1, -2)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{AD} = D - A = (6 - 3, -7 - (-4), 3 - 2) = (3, -3, 1)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we compute the cross product \(\vec{AB} \times \vec{AC}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 & -4 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 & 1 & -2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} = \mathbf{i} \left( (-4)(-2) - (3)(1) \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( (2)(-2) - (3)(1) \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( (2)(1) - (-4)(1) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \mathbf{i} (8 - 3) - \mathbf{j} (-4 - 3) + \mathbf{k} (2 + 4)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \mathbf{i} (5) - \mathbf{j} (-7) + \mathbf{k} (6)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 5\mathbf{i} + 7\mathbf{j} + 6\mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = (5, 7, 6)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we compute the magnitude of this vector:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left\| \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} \right\| = \sqrt{5^2 + 7^2 + 6^2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{25 + 49 + 36}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{110}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, we find the area of the quadrilateral:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{110}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the area of the quadrilateral is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{\sqrt{110}}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
