[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} a \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\), we use the formula for the projection of a vector \(\mathbf{v}\) onto a vector \(\mathbf{u}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{u}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}}{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u}} \mathbf{u}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we compute the dot product \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u} = a \cdot (-1) + 7 \cdot 4 = -a + 28
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we compute the dot product \(\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u} = (-1)^2 + 4^2 = 1 + 16 = 17
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we substitute these values into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{u}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{-a + 28}{17} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We are given that the projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{u}\) is \(\frac{26}{17} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\). Therefore, we can set up the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{-a + 28}{17} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{26}{17} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m By comparing the scalar factors, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{-a + 28}{17} = \frac{26}{17}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can cancel the 17 on both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - a + 28 = 26
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we solve for \(a\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - a + 28 = 26
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract 28 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - a = 26 - 28
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - a = -2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Multiply both sides by -1:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a = 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the value of \(a\) is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
