[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To compute \(\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 8 \end{pmatrix}\), we will use the definition of the dot product. The dot product of two vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} c \\ d \end{pmatrix}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} c \\ d \end{pmatrix} = ac + bd
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Here, the vectors are \(\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 8 \end{pmatrix}\). So, we will compute the product of the components as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 8 \end{pmatrix} = (-4)(6) + (-1)(8)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (-4)(6) = -24
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (-1)(8) = -8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we add these products together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -24 + (-8) = -24 - 8 = -32
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the dot product of \(\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 8 \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-32}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
