[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the units digit of \(9^{8^7}\), we need to determine the pattern in the units digits of the powers of 9. Let's start by examining the first few powers of 9:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9^1 = 9 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9^2 = 81 \quad \text{(units digit is 1)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9^3 = 729 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9^4 = 6561 \quad \text{(units digit is 1)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9^5 = 59049 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can see that the units digits repeat every 2 powers: 9, 1, 9, 1, ... In other words, the units digit of \(9^n\) cycles through 0, 1, 9 in the cycle of 2 numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to determine the exponent \(8^7\) modulo 2 (since the cycle lengths are 2, we only need to look at 1 numbers in the cycle). 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's calculate \(8^7 \mod 2\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 8 \mod 2 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, \(8^7 \equiv 0 \pmod{2}\). This means that the units digit of \(9^{8^7}\) will be the same as the units digit of \(9^0\), which is 9.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the units digit of \(9^{8^7}\) is \(\boxed{9}\).<|endoftext|>
