[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To convert the hexadecimal number \(\rm{A03}_{16}\) to a base 10 integer, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Convert each hexadecimal digit to its decimal equivalent.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Sum the decimal equivalents of all the digits.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's start with the hexadecimal number \(\rm{A03}_{16}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The hexadecimal digit \(A\) represents 10 in decimal.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The hexadecimal digit \(0\) represents 0 in decimal.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The hexadecimal digit \(3\) represents 3 in decimal.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we will convert each hexadecimal digit to base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A = 10_{16} \rightarrow 10 \times 16^0 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 = 0_{16} \rightarrow 0 \times 16^0 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3 = 3_{16} \rightarrow 3 \times 16^1 = 3 \times 16 = 48_{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we sum all the decimal equivalents:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 10 + 0 + 48 = 58
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the base 10 integer representation of \(\rm{A03}_{16}\) is \(\boxed{58}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
