[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Peter is having a party on Saturday and wants to serve 60 Christmas side-dishes and 100 Eggplant telebollons. He expects that each guest will serve an average of 8 other dishes. If he invites 30 guests and if he sells the rest as Christmas trees, at $30 each, how much money will he raise?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how much money Peter will raise, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of dishes Peter needs to serve during the party.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Determine the total number of guests Peter invites.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Calculate the total number of dishes that will be sold, given that he will sell the rest as Christmas trees.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Calculate the total revenue from selling the dishes at $30 each.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Firstly, the total number of dishes Peter needs to serve is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 60 \text{ Christmas side-dishes} + 100 \text{ Eggplant telebollons} = 160 \text{ dishes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, the total number of guests Peter invites is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 30 \text{ guests} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The number of dishes that will be sold is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 160 \text{ dishes} \times 8 \text{ dishes per guest} = 1280 \text{ dishes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The remaining dishes will be sold as Christmas trees:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 160 \text{ dishes} - 1280 \text{ dishes} = 0 \text{ dishes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the rest of the dishes are sold as Christmas trees, and we are assuming that we are selling them entirely as Christmas trees, the total revenue is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 0 \text{ Christmas trees} \times \$30 \text{ per Christmas tree} = \$0 \text{ revenue} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the total money Peter will raise is:
