[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the given polynomial equation \(x^4 - 3x^3 + 5x^2 - 27x - 36 = 0\), we can use the Rational Root Theorem to find potential rational roots. The Rational Root Theorem states that any potential rational root, expressed in its lowest terms as \(\frac{p}{q}\), must have \(p\) as a factor of the constant term (here, \(-36\)) and \(q\) as a factor of the leading coefficient (here, \(1\)).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The factors of \(-36\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 3, \pm 4, \pm 6, \pm 9, \pm 12, \pm 18, \pm 36
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The factors of \(1\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \pm 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the possible rational roots are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 3, \pm 4, \pm 6, \pm 9, \pm 12, \pm 18, \pm 36
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We will test these possible roots by substituting them into the polynomial and checking if they yield zero.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Testing \(x = 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^4 - 3 \cdot 3^3 + 5 \cdot 3^2 - 27 \cdot 3 - 36 = 81 - 81 + 45 - 81 - 36 = -121 \neq 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Testing \(x = -3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (-3)^4 - 3 \cdot (-3)^3 + 5 \cdot (-3)^2 - 27 \cdot (-3) - 36 = 81 + 81 + 45 + 81 - 36 = 246 \neq 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Testing \(x = 2\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2^4 - 3 \cdot 2^3 + 5 \cdot 2^2 - 27 \cdot 2 - 36 = 16 - 24 + 20 - 54 - 36 = -84 \neq 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Testing \(x = -2\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (-2)^4 - 3 \cdot (-2)^3 + 5 \cdot (-2)^2 - 27 \cdot (-2) - 36 = 16 + 24 + 20 + 54 - 36 = 79 \neq 0
