[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the product of the divisors of \(50\), we first need to determine all of its divisors. The number \(50\) can be factored into prime factors as \(50 = 2 \times 5^2\). The divisors of \(50\) are therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[1, 2, 5, 10, 25, 50\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we calculate the product of these divisors. We can break this down step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 \times 2 &= 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 \times 5 &= 10 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 10 \times 25 &= 250 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 25 \times 50 &= 1250 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 \times 5 \times 10 &= 100 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5 \times 10 \times 25 &= 1250 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 10 \times 25 \times 5 &= 1250 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 25 \times 50 \times 1 &= 1250 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we sum these products together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 + 10 + 250 + 1250 + 100 + 1250 + 1250 + 1250
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's add these step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 + 10 = 12 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 12 + 250 = 262 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 262 + 1250 = 1512 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1512 + 100 = 1612 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1612 + 1250 = 2862 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2862 + 1250 = 4112 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4112 + 1250 = 5362 \\
