[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's rewrite the given complex numbers in their exponential form:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[3 \operatorname{cis} 18^\circ = 3 (\cos 18^\circ + i \sin 18^\circ)\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-2 \operatorname{cis} 37^\circ = -2 (\cos 37^\circ + i \sin 37^\circ)\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we multiply these two complex numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[(3 \operatorname{cis} 18^\circ)(-2 \operatorname{cis} 37^\circ) = (3 \cos 18^\circ + 3i \sin 18^\circ)(-2 \cos 37^\circ - 2i \sin 37^\circ)\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can simplify this by distributing \(\cos 37^\circ\) and \(\sin 37^\circ\) across their respective terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[(3 \cos 18^\circ)(-2 \cos 37^\circ) + (3 \cos 18^\circ)(-2i \sin 37^\circ) + (3i \sin 18^\circ)(-2 \cos 37^\circ) + (3i \sin 18^\circ)(-2i \sin 37^\circ)\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify each term:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-6 \cos 18^\circ \cos 37^\circ - 6i \cos 18^\circ \sin 37^\circ - 6i \sin 18^\circ \cos 37^\circ - 6i^2 \sin 37^\circ\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Recall that \(i^2 = -1\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-6 \cos 18^\circ \cos 37^\circ - 6i \cos 18^\circ \sin 37^\circ - 6i \sin 18^\circ \cos 37^\circ + 6\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Group the real and imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-6 (\cos 18^\circ \cos 37^\circ + i \cos 18^\circ \sin 37^\circ) + 6 (\sin 18^\circ \cos 37^\circ - i \sin 18^\circ \sin 37^\circ)\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m These can be factored further using the sinusoidal identity for the product of cosines and sines:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[-6 \cos (18^\circ + 37^\circ) + 6 \sin (18^\circ - 37^\circ) + 6 \sin (18^\circ - 37^\circ)i\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
