[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find what fraction of \(\frac{1}{2}\) is \(\frac{1}{7}\), we need to divide \(\frac{1}{7}\) by \(\frac{1}{2}\). Dividing by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying by its reciprocal. The reciprocal of \(\frac{1}{2}\) is \(2\). Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{1}{7} \div \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{7} \times 2 = \frac{2}{7}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, \(\frac{1}{7}\) is \(\frac{2}{7}\) of \(\frac{1}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The answer is \(\boxed{\frac{2}{7}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
