[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Evaluate
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\begin{vmatrix} \cos \alpha \cos \beta & \cos \alpha \sin \beta & -\sin \alpha \\ -\sin \beta & \cos \beta & 0 \\ \sin \alpha \cos \beta & \sin \alpha \sin \beta & \cos \alpha \end{vmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To evaluate the determinant of the given matrix, we will use the formula for the determinant of a 3x3 matrix. The determinant of a matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{vmatrix}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a(ei - fh) - b(di - fg) + c(dh - eg)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For the given matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} \cos \alpha \cos \beta & \cos \alpha \sin \beta & -\sin \alpha \\ -\sin \beta & \cos \beta & 0 \\ \sin \alpha \cos \beta & \sin \alpha \sin \beta & \cos \alpha \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We identify the elements as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(a = \cos \alpha \cos \beta\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(b = \cos \alpha \sin \beta\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(c = -\sin \alpha\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(d = -\sin \beta\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(e = \cos \beta\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(f = 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(g = \sin \alpha \cos \beta\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(h = \sin \alpha \sin \beta\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(i = \cos \alpha\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now apply the determinant formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} \cos \alpha \cos \beta & \cos \alpha \sin \beta & -\sin \alpha \\ -\sin \beta & \cos \beta & 0 \\ \sin \alpha \cos \beta & \sin \alpha \sin \beta & \cos \alpha \end{vmatrix} = \cos \alpha \cos \beta (\cos \beta \cos \alpha - 0 \cdot \sin \alpha \sin \beta) - \cos \alpha \sin \beta (-\sin \beta \cos \alpha) - \sin \alpha (-\sin \beta \sin \beta \cos \beta)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify each term:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. First term:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \cos \alpha \cos \beta (\cos \beta \cos \alpha)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since \(\cos \beta \cos \alpha\) is the product of \(\cos \alpha\) and \(\cos \beta\) with opposite signs:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \cos \alpha \cos \beta \cos \alpha \cos \beta = (\cos \alpha \cos \beta \cos \alpha) (\cos \beta \cos \alpha) = (\cos \alpha \cos \alpha \cdot \cos \beta \cos \beta) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Second term:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \cos \alpha \sin \beta \sin \beta \cos \alpha
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Using the angle subtraction formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \sin 2\beta = 2 \sin \beta \cos \beta \implies \sin^2 2\beta = (\sin \beta \cos \beta)^2 = \sin^2 \beta \cos^2 \beta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \cos^2 2\beta = 1 - \sin^2 2\beta = 1 - \sin^2 \beta \cos^2 \beta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \cos \alpha \sin \beta \sin \beta \cos \alpha = \sin^2 \beta \cos^2 \beta \cos \alpha \implies \frac{1}{2} \sin 2\beta \cos 2\beta = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{1}{2} \sin 2\beta \cos 2\beta = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Third term:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \sin \alpha \sin \beta \sin \beta \cos \beta = \sin^2 \beta \cos^2 \beta \sin^2 \beta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \sin^2 \beta \cos^2 \beta \sin^2 \beta = \left(\frac{1}{2} \sin 2\beta \right)^2 \sin^2 \beta \cos^2 \beta = \frac{1}{4} \sin^2 2\beta \cos^2 \beta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since \(\sin 2\beta = 2 \sin \beta \cos \beta\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{1}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{2} \sin 4\beta = \frac{1}{8} \sin 4\beta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combining all terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0 + 0 + \frac{1}{8} \sin 4\beta = \frac{1}{8} \sin 4\beta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the determinant of the matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{8} \sin 4\beta}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{1}{8}\sin4\beta
