[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the value of \(6 \& 3\) using the operation \(\&\) defined as \((a \& b) = (a + b)(a - b)\), we need to substitute \(a = 6\) and \(b = 3\) into the expression.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we calculate the sum \(a + b\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 + 3 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we calculate the difference \(a - b\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 - 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we substitute these values back into the expression \((a \& b) = (a + b)(a - b)\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 \& 3 = 9 \cdot 3 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \(6 \& 3\) is \(\boxed{27}\).<|endoftext|>
