[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \(1 - 0.\overline{9}\), we first need to understand the repeating decimal \(0.\overline{9}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This decimal represents the fraction \(\frac{9}{99}\) because the digits "9" repeatedly form a cycle in the decimal representation. Let's convert \(\frac{9}{99}\) to its simplest form.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{9}{99} = \frac{9}{9 \times 11} = \frac{1}{11}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, \(0.\overline{9}\) is equal to \(\frac{1}{11}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we want to find \(1 - \frac{1}{11}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 - \frac{1}{11} = \frac{11}{11} - \frac{1}{11} = \frac{11 - 1}{11} = \frac{10}{11}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \(1 - 0.\overline{9}\) is \(\boxed{\frac{10}{11}}\).<|endoftext|>
