[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the minimum score Fisher must earn in the fourth quarter to have an average of at least 83% over all four quarters, we can set up the following equation based on the formula for the average:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Average score} = \frac{\text{Sum of the scores}}{\text{Total number of quarters}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In this problem:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The total number of quarters is 4.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Fisher's scores in the first three quarters are 82%, 77%, and 75%.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let \( x \) be the score Fisher earns in the fourth quarter. The sum of the scores in all four quarters is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 82 + 77 + 75 + x
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need the average score to be at least 83%, which corresponds to a total of \( 4 \times 100 = 400 \) units of score. Therefore, we can set up the following inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{82 + 77 + 75 + x}{4} \geq 83
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, simplify the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 82 + 77 + 75 + x = 234 + x
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, substitute this back into the inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{234 + x}{4} \geq 83
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides of the inequality by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 234 + x \geq 332
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, isolate \( x \) by subtracting 234 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x \geq 98
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the minimum score Fisher must earn in the fourth quarter to have an average of at least 83% over all four quarters is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{98}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
