[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To convert the point \((\rho, \theta, \phi) = \left( 12, \frac{7\pi}{6}, \frac{\pi}{3} \right)\) from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we use the following formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \rho \sin \phi \cos \theta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m y = \rho \sin \phi \sin \theta
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m z = \rho \cos \phi
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \rho = 12, \quad \theta = \frac{7\pi}{6}, \quad \phi = \frac{\pi}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, calculate \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = 12 \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) \cos \left( \frac{7\pi}{6} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos \left( \frac{7\pi}{6} \right) = \cos \left( 2\pi - \frac{\pi}{6} \right) = \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{6} \right) = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute these values into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = 12 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} = 12 \cdot \frac{3}{4} = 9
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, calculate \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m y = 12 \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) \sin \left( \frac{7\pi}{6} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We already know:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \sin \left( \frac{7\pi}{6} \right) = -\sin \left( \frac{\pi}{6} \right) = -\frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute these values into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m y = 12 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cdot -\frac{1}{2} = 12 \cdot \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \right) = -3\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, calculate \(z\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m z = 12 \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute this value into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m z = 12 \cdot \frac{1}{2} = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the rectangular coordinates are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{(9, -3\sqrt{3}, 6)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
