[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Find $\cot 45^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Sure, let's find \(\cot 45^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The cotangent of an angle \(\theta\) is defined as the reciprocal of the tangent of that angle. That is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cot \theta = \frac{1}{\tan \theta}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to find \(\cot 45^\circ\). So we substitute \(\theta = 45^\circ\) into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cot 45^\circ = \frac{1}{\tan 45^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know that \(\tan 45^\circ = 1\), so:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cot 45^\circ = \frac{1}{1} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\cot 45^\circ\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
