[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the number of obtuse interior angles in an obtuse triangle, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the properties of an obtuse triangle**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - An obtuse triangle is a triangle that has one obtuse angle (an angle greater than 90 degrees).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Recall the definition of an obtuse angle**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - An angle is obtuse if it is greater than 90 degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Consider the sum of angles in any triangle**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always 180 degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Determine the relationship between angles in an obtuse triangle**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - In any triangle, the sum of the interior angles is always greater than 180 degrees. Therefore, if an obtuse triangle has three angles, at least one of these angles must be obtuse.
