[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the semi-minor axis of the ellipse, we need to use the properties of an ellipse. The standard form of an ellipse centered at \((-3, 1)\) with the equation \(\frac{(x + 3)^2}{b^2} + \frac{(y - 1)^2}{a^2} = 1\), where \(a\) is the semi-major axis and \(b\) is the semi-minor axis, is maximized when the semi-major axis \(a\) (and subsequently the semi-minor axis \(b\)) is minimized.
