[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m What is the units digit of $3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the units digit of the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\), we need to analyze the pattern in the units digits of the powers of 3.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's list the first few powers of 3:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^1 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^2 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^3 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^4 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^5 = 243
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We observe that the units digits of the powers of 3 repeat every 4 terms: 3, 9, 7, 1. Therefore, the units digit of \(3^n\) depends on the remainder when \(n\) is divided by 4. Let's find this remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^1 \equiv 3 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^2 \equiv 9 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^3 \equiv 7 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The pattern repeats every 4 terms. To find the units digit of \(3^n\) for any \(n\), we need to determine the position of \(n\) in the cycle. We do this by finding the remainder when \(n\) is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n \equiv 1, 2, 3, 0 \pmod{4}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The units digit of \(3^n\) corresponds to the remainder when \(n\) is divided by 4. We have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n \equiv 1 \text{ (mod 4)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n \equiv 2 \text{ (mod 4)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n \equiv 3 \text{ (mod 4)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n \equiv 0 \text{ (mod 4)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, \(n\) can be classified as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
