[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m for some integer \(k\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's focus on the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can pair the terms as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (3^1 + 3^{2019}) + (3^3 + 3^{2017}) + (3^5 + 3^{2015}) + \ldots + (3^{2009} + 3^{1})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Each pair \(3^1 + 3^{2019}\), \(3^3 + 3^{2017}\), \(3^5 + 3^{2015}\), \ldots, \(3^{2009} + 3^{1}\) results in a units digit of:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^1 \times 3^{2019} \equiv 3^1 \equiv 3 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^3 \times 3^{2017} \equiv 3^3 \equiv 27 \equiv 7 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^5 \times 3^{2015} \equiv 3^5 \equiv 243 \equiv 3 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vdots
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^{2009} \times 3^1 \equiv 3^{2009} \equiv 1005002536 \pmod{10} \equiv 6 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Summing these units digits:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3 + 7 + 3 + 3 + \ldots + 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This is an arithmetic series with first term 3, last term 6, and \(n = 2009\). The number of terms is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2009
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The sum of an arithmetic series is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Sum} = \frac{n}{2} \times (\text{first term} + \text{last term})
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Sum} = \frac{2009}{2} \times (3 + 6) = \frac{2009}{2} \times 9 = 2009 \times 4.5 = 9040.5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The units digit of the sum is the remainder when 9040.5 is divided by 10:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9040.5 \equiv 0.5 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0.5 = 0.5 \times 10
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Units digit} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the units digit of \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{0}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
