[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. The digits can only be 0 or 1 (since the numbers 0 and 1 don't involve the digit \(-1\)), so \( b \) can only be 1 (as 0 is not possible).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m However, since we need \( b \) to be the only digit in an unbounded base, the only possible answer is \( b = 1 \).
