[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, there is only one multiple of 9 within the range of 1 to 200 that leaves a remainder of 1 when divided by 9. Therefore, there is only one integer from the first 200 positive integers that is congruent to 1 modulo 9.
