[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the common factor:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    First, we look for the greatest common factor (GCF) of the coefficients and the variables in the expression.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The coefficients are 46 and 115. The GCF of 46 and 115 is 13.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The variables are \(x^3\) and \(x^7\). The GCF of \(x^3\) and \(x^7\) is \(x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore, the GCF of the entire expression is \(13x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Factor out the GCF:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We factor out \(13x^3\) from each term in the expression.
