[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the given equation \( |{-2y}| \cdot |{-\dfrac{y}{2}}| = 36 \), we will break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, simplify the absolute values:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ |{-2y}| = 2|y| \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ |{-\dfrac{y}{2}}| = \dfrac{|y|}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute these back into the original equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 2|y| \cdot \dfrac{|y|}{2} = 36 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \dfrac{2|y| \cdot |y|}{2} = 36 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \dfrac{2|y|^2}{2} = 36 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ |y|^2 = 36 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve for \( |y| \), take the square root of both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ |y| = \sqrt{36} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ |y| = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This gives us two possible values for \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ y = 6 \quad \text{or} \quad y = -6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to find the product of these values of \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 6 \cdot (-6) = -36 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the product of all real values of \( y \) that satisfy the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-36}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -36
