[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let $S$ be the set of points $z$ in the complex plane such that $|z - 7 + 10i| \le 5.$  Find the area of $S.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the area of the set \( S \) in the complex plane, we need to determine the region defined by the inequality \( |z - 7 + 10i| \le 5 \). This inequality describes a disk centered at \( 7 - 10i \) with a radius of 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The disk \( |z - 7 + 10i| \le 5 \) can be visualized as a circular region centered at \( 7 - 10i \) with a radius of 5. When we consider the intersection of this disk with the real axis (i.e., the real number line), the area of the disk is given by the area under the parabola \( y = z^2 \) where \( z \) is a real number, from \( z = 7 - 10i \) (the center) to \( z = 7 + 10i \) (the right boundary).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The area under the parabola \( y = z^2 \) from \( z = 7 - 10i \) to \( z = 7 + 10i \) can be calculated using the formula for the area under a curve from \( x = a \) to \( x = b \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \int_{a}^{b} y \, dx = \int_{7-10i}^{7+10i} z^2 \, dz
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we find the width of the disk along the real axis:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \Delta z = (7 + 10i) - (7 - 10i) = 20i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The integrated area is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \int_{7-10i}^{7+10i} z^2 \, dz = \left[ \frac{z^3}{3} \right]_{7-10i}^{7+10i}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Evaluating this at the limits:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left. \frac{z^3}{3} \right|_{7-10i}^{7+10i} = \frac{(7+10i)^3}{3} - \frac{(7-10i)^3}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We expand \( (7+10i)^3 \) and \( (7-10i)^3 \) using the binomial theorem:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (7+10i)^3 = \binom{3}{1} (7)^2 (10i) + \binom{3}{2} (7)^2 (10i)^2 + \binom{3}{3} (7)^2 (10i)^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 3 \cdot 49 \cdot 10i + 3 \cdot 49 \cdot 100i^2 + 1 \cdot 49 \cdot 1000i^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 1470i + 14700i^2 - 49000i^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \( i^2 = -1 \) and \( i^3 = i \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 1470i - 14700(-1) - 49000i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 1470i + 14700 + 49000i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 14700 + 49470i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Similarly, for \( (7-10i)^3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (7-10i)^3 = \binom{3}{1} (7)^2 (-10i) + \binom{3}{2} (7)^2 (-10i)^2 + \binom{3}{3} (7)^2 (-10i)^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 3 \cdot 49 \cdot (-10i) + 3 \cdot 49 \cdot 100i^2 + 1 \cdot 49 \cdot (-1000i^3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = -1470i - 14700i^2 - 49000i^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Again, using \( i^2 = -1 \) and \( i^3 = i \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = -1470i - 14700(-1) - 49000i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = -1470i + 14700 - 49000i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 14700 - 48370i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtracting these two results:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \left( \frac{14700 + 49470i}{3} \right) - \left( \frac{14700 - 48370i}{3} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \frac{14700 + 49470i - 14700 + 48370i}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \frac{97740i}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 32580i
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \( y = z^2 \) is always non-negative, the area under the disk is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{32580}
