[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many of the given infinite list of numbers are integers, we need to understand the definitions of both integer and irrational numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - An integer is a whole number (positive, negative, or zero) that can be written as \( n \in \mathbb{Z} \), where \( n \) is an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - An irrational number is a number that cannot be expressed as a simple fraction and has decimal places that neither terminate nor repeat.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The list provided is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
