[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the overall percentage of people surveyed who support increased funding, we need to use the weighted average of the support percentages for men and women. The study surveyed 100 men and 900 women, and 80% of men and 60% of women support increased funding.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The formula for the total support percentage is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Total Support Percentage} = (\text{Support Percentage of Men} \times \text{Number of Men}) + (\text{Support Percentage of Women} \times \text{Number of Women})
