[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the greatest common factor (GCF) of the terms.**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The terms are \(2x^2y\), \(-8xy\), and \(8y\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The GCF of the coefficients \(2\), \(-8\), and \(8\) is \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The GCF of the variables \(x^2y\), \(-8xy\), and \(8y\) is \(xy\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Therefore, the GCF of the entire expression is \(2xy\).
