[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m which gives us:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f^{-1}(x) = x \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we have \( f(2) = b \) and \( f^{-1}(b+1) \). Since \( f^{-1}(x) = x \), it follows that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f^{-1}(b+1) = b+1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We are given that \( f(2) = f^{-1}(b+1) \), so:
