[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the second-smallest three-digit palindromic prime number, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Understand the definition**: A three-digit palindromic number reads the same forwards and backwards. The smallest three-digit palindromic number is 101.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Identify the next palindrome**: The next palindrome after 101 is 111.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Check 111 for primality**: To determine if 111 is a prime number, we need to check if it has any divisors other than 1 and itself. We will check divisibility by all prime numbers up to the square root of 111.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 111**: \(111 \div 1\) (not prime)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 55**: \(55 \div 5\) (divisibility by 5)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 33**: \(33 \div 3\) (divisibility by 3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 11**: \(11\) (divisibility by 11)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 11**: \(11\) (divisibility by 11)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore, 111 is not a prime number because it has divisors other than 1 and itself.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Find the next smallest three-digit palindromic prime**: Since 111 is not a prime, we move to the next palindrome, 110.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Check 110 for primality**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 110**: \(110 \div 2\) (not prime)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 55**: \(55 \div 5\) (divisibility by 5)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 33**: \(33 \div 3\) (divisibility by 3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 11**: \(11\) (divisibility by 11)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - **Divisors of 11**: \(11\) (divisibility by 11)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Therefore, 110 is a prime number because it has no divisors other than 1 and itself.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. **Conclusion**: The second-smallest three-digit palindromic prime number is 110.
