[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A round-robin tennis tournament consists of each player playing every other player exactly once.  How many matches will be held during an 8-person round-robin tennis tournament?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the total number of matches in an eight-person round-robin tennis tournament, we can use the concept of combinations. In a round-robin tournament with \( n \) players, each player plays every other player exactly once. The number of matches is given by the combination formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \binom{n}{2} = \frac{n(n-1)}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For an eight-person tournament (\( n = 8 \)):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \binom{8}{2} = \frac{8 \times (8-1)}{2} = \frac{8 \times 7}{2} = \frac{56}{2} = 28
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the total number of matches held during an eight-person round-robin tennis tournament is \(\boxed{28}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 28
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
