[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Lyndy conducted a survey of the 300 students in her school. She found that 60 students own dogs, while only 30 students own cats. What percent of the students own cats?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the percentage of students who own cats, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Identify the total number of students surveyed.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Total number of students = 300
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Identify the number of students who own cats.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Number of students who own cats = 30
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Calculate the percentage of students who own cats.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The formula to find the percentage is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Percentage} = \left( \frac{\text{Number of students who own cats}}{\text{Total number of students}} \right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Substituting the given values:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Percentage} = \left( \frac{30}{300} \right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{30}{300} = \frac{1}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So, the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Percentage} = \left( \frac{1}{10} \right) \times 100 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the percentage of students who own cats is \boxed{10}.<|endoftext|>
