[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \( f(g(3)) \), we need to evaluate the functions \( f \) and \( g \) step by step, starting with \( g(3) \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we evaluate \( g(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ g(x) = 2x^2 - 2x - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ g(3) = 2(3)^2 - 2(3) - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ g(3) = 2(9) - 6 - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ g(3) = 18 - 6 - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ g(3) = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now that we have \( g(3) = 9 \), we need to evaluate \( f(9) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(x) = 2\sqrt{x} + \frac{12}{\sqrt{x}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(9) = 2\sqrt{9} + \frac{12}{\sqrt{9}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(9) = 2 \cdot 3 + \frac{12}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(9) = 6 + 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f(9) = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( f(g(3)) \) is \(\boxed{10}\).<|endoftext|>
