[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the sum of the two vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the definition of the dot product. The dot product of two vectors \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\ a_2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\ b_2 \end{pmatrix}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Here, \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\). Substituting the values into the dot product formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = (-3)(-2) + (5)(1)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (-3)(-2) = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (5)(1) = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Adding these results together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 + 5 = 11
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the sum of the two vectors is \(\boxed{11}\).<|endoftext|>
