[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 3: Use the Rational Root Theorem method
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The Rational Root Theorem tells us that any rational root of the polynomial is a factor of the constant term divided by the leading coefficient. For the first polynomial \(2x^3 + x^2 - 8x + 20 = 0\), the possible rational roots are \(\pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 4, \pm 5, \pm 10, \pm 20\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We test these possible roots:
