[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \( y \), we need to determine the projection of vector \(\mathbf{v}\) onto vector \(\mathbf{w}\). The formula for the projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
