[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = 1 \cdot 9 + y \cdot 3 = 9 + 3y
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w} = 9 \cdot 9 + 3 \cdot 3 = 81 + 9 = 90
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting these into the projection formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{9 + 3y}{90} \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{9 + 3y}{10} \\ \frac{3(9 + 3y)}{90} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{9 + 3y}{10} \\ \frac{3(3 + y)}{30} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{9 + 3y}{10} \\ \frac{9 + 3y}{10} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{9 + 3y}{10} \\ \frac{9 + 3y}{10} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We are given that the projection is \(\begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\), so we can set up the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{9 + 3y}{10} = -6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{9 + 3y}{10} = -2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m From the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9 + 3y = -60
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3y = -69
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m y = -23
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can verify this value by substituting \( y = -23 \) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{9 + 3(-23)}{10} = \frac{9 - 69}{10} = \frac{-60}{10} = -6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This is consistent with the first equation, confirming that our solution is correct.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( y \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-23}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
