[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Anna ran 6 kilometers. IF she decided to run twice as far in half the time, how many minutes would it have taken her if she ran at 5 km/h?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how long it would have taken Anna to run 6 kilometers at a speed of 5 km/h, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Calculate the time it takes to run 6 kilometers at a speed of 5 km/h:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{6 \text{ km}}{5 \text{ km/h}} = 1.2 \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Convert the time from hours to minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we multiply the time in hours by 60:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1.2 \text{ hours} \times 60 \text{ minutes/hour} = 72 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, it would have taken Anna \(\boxed{72}\) minutes to run 6 kilometers at a speed of 5 km/h.
