[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If $x$, $y$, and $z$ are real numbers for which  \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x+y-z &= -8, \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x-y+z &= 18,\text{ and} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -x+y+z &= 30, \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{align*} then what is $xyz$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve for \(x\), \(y\), and \(z\) given the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y - z = -8, \quad x - y + z = 18, \quad -x + y + z = 30
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m we can add all three equations together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x + y - z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) = -8 + 18 + 30
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying the left side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y - z + x - y + z - x + y + z = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the sum of the equations is 0. This means:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -x + y + z = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can solve this equation for \(z\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -x + y + z = 0 \implies z = x - y
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we substitute \(z = x - y\) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y - (x - y) = -8 \implies x + y - x + y = -8 \implies 2y = -8 \implies y = -4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we substitute \(y = -4\) and \(z = x - y\) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x - (-4) + (x - (-4)) = 18 \implies x + 4 + x - (-4) = 18 \implies 2x + 8 = 18 \implies 2x = 10 \implies x = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now that we have \(x = 5\), \(y = -4\), and \(z = 5 - (-4) = 9\), we can find the product \(xyz\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m xyz = 5 \cdot (-4) \cdot 9 = 180
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the value of \(xyz\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{180}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
