[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To expand the expression \((2x+3)(x+5)\), we will use the distributive property, also known as the FOIL method (First, Outer, Inner, Last) for binomials.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 1: Distribute \(2x\) to \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[2x \cdot x = 2x^2\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 2: Distribute \(2x\) to \(5\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[2x \cdot 5 = 10x\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 3: Distribute \(3\) to \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[3 \cdot x = 3x\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Step 4: Distribute \(3\) to \(5\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[3 \cdot 5 = 15\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, combine all these results:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combine the like terms \(10x\) and \(3x\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[2x^2 + 13x + 15\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the expanded form of \((2x+3)(x+5)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\]<|endoftext|>
