[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The equation of line \( n \) is \( y = kx - 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The line \( m \) intersects the line \( n \) at the point \((-4, -7)\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Substitute the coordinates of the intersection point into the equations:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The \( x \)-coordinate of the intersection point is \(-4\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Substitute \( x = -4 \) into the equation of line \( m \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      -7 = 3(-4) + 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      -7 = -12 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      -7 = -7
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      This confirms that the point \((-4, -7)\) is correct for both lines.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Substitute the coordinates of the intersection point into the equation of line \( n \):**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The \( y \)-coordinate of the intersection point is \(-7\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Substitute \( y = -7 \) into the equation of line \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      -7 = k(-4) - 7
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      -7 = -4k - 7
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      Add 7 to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      0 = -4k
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      Divide both sides by \(-4\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      k = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( k \) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
