[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A population of bacteria is doubling every four hours. At noon there are $600$ bacteria. If this rate continues, how many bacteria will be present at midnight, twelve hours later?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the number of bacteria present at midnight, we need to understand the exponential growth pattern of the bacteria population. The bacteria population doubles every 4 hours. 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Initial population at noon: \( 600 \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - Time interval: 12 hours
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, calculate the number of 4-hour intervals in 12 hours:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{12 \text{ hours}}{4 \text{ hours/interval}} = 3 \text{ intervals}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we use the formula for exponential growth:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m N = N_0 \times 2^t
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( N \) is the final population at time \( t \)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( N_0 \) is the initial population
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( t \) is the time
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute the known values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m N = 600 \times 2^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Calculate \( 2^3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2^3 = 8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, multiply the initial population by 8:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m N = 600 \times 8 = 4800
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the number of bacteria present at midnight is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{4800}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4800
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
