[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To rationalize the denominator of \(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{7}}\), we need to eliminate the square root from the denominator. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Identify the denominator: \(2\sqrt{7}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Multiply both the numerator and the denominator by \(\sqrt{7}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
