[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Five members of a family play hockey.  Four of them are all twins with the same height.  The fifth member is 160 cm tall.  The average height of the family is 155 cm.  How tall is the twins?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the heights of the twins, we need to use the information given and set up equations accordingly.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Let the heights of the 5 family members be \( h_1, h_2, h_3, h_4, \) and \( h_5 \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    h_1 = h_2 = \text{height of twins (since they are twins)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    h_3 = h_4 = 160 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    h_5 = \text{height of the twins}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. The family average height is given as 155 cm. The total height of all 5 family members can be expressed as the sum of their individual heights:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    155 \times 5 = 775 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. The sum of the individual heights is also equal to 775 cm. Therefore, the sum of the heights of the twins \( h_1 \), \( h_2 \), \( h_3 \), and \( h_4 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    h_1 + h_2 + h_3 + h_4 = 775 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Since \( h_1 = h_2 = 160 \), we can substitute these values into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    160 + 160 + h_3 + h_4 = 775
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. Subtract 320 from both sides of the equation (subtracting \( h_3 + h_4 \) from \( 160 + 160 \)):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    160 + 160 - 320 = h_3 + h_4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    40 = h_3 + h_4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. We also know from the problem statement that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    h_3 = 40 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 7. Therefore, the heights of the twins are:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \boxed{40 \text{ cm and } 160 \text{ cm}}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
