[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Find the area of the triangle with vertices $(0,7,10),$ $(-1,6,6),$ and $(-4,9,6).$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the area of the triangle with vertices \((0,7,10)\), \((-1,6,6)\), and \((-4,9,6)\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle in 3D space:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left\| \vec{A B} \times \vec{A C} \right\|
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \(\vec{A B}\) and \(\vec{A C}\) are vectors that form the sides of the triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's define the vectors \(\vec{A B}\) and \(\vec{A C}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{A B} = (-1 - 0, 6 - 7, 6 - 10) = (-1, -1, -4)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{A C} = (-4 - 0, 9 - 7, 6 - 10) = (-4, 2, -4)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we need to find the cross product \(\vec{A B} \times \vec{A C}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{A B} \times \vec{A C} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -1 & -1 & -4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -4 & 2 & -4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \vec{A B} \times \vec{A C} = \mathbf{i} \left( (-1)(-4) - (-4)(2) \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( (-1)(-4) - (-4)(-4) \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( (-1)(2) - (-1)(-4) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \mathbf{i} (4 + 8) - \mathbf{j} (4 - 16) + \mathbf{k} (-2 - 4)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 12\mathbf{i} - 12\mathbf{j} - 6\mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = (12, -12, -6)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to find the magnitude of this vector:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \left\| \vec{A B} \times \vec{A C} \right\| = \sqrt{12^2 + (-12)^2 + (-6)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{144 + 144 + 36}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{324}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 18
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, we can find the area of the triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 18 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the area of the triangle is \(\boxed{9}\).<|endoftext|>
