[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For what ordered pair $(a,b)$ are there infinite solutions $(x,y)$ to the system \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2ax+2y&=b,\\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5x+y&=-3?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve for the ordered pair \((a, b)\) in the system of equations
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2ax + 2y = b
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5x + y = -3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m we will use the method of elimination. First, we can eliminate \(y\) by subtracting the second equation from the first equation. This will give us an equation involving \(a\) only:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2ax + 2y - (5x + y) = b - (-3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2ax + 2y - 5x - y = b + 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (2a - 5)x + y = b + 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \((a, b)\) is an ordered pair, we can express \(x\) in terms of \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \frac{b + 3 - y}{2a - 5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \(x\) to be an integer for all \(y\), \(\frac{b + 3 - y}{2a - 5}\) must always be an integer. This implies that \(2a - 5\) must divide \(b + 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we will eliminate \(x\) by using the second equation. Multiply the second equation by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 10x + 2y = -6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, subtract the first equation \(2ax + 2y = b\) from this equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (10x + 2y) - (2ax + 2y) = -6 - (b + 3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 10x + 2y - 2ax - 2y = -6 - b - 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (10 - 2a)x = -9 - b
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Solve for \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \frac{-9 - b}{10 - 2a}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For \(x\) to be an integer, \(\frac{-9 - b}{10 - 2a}\) must be an integer. This implies that \(10 - 2a\) must divide \(-9 - b\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We now have a system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \frac{-9 - b}{2a - 5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = \frac{9 + b}{10 - 2a}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Equating the two expressions for \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{-9 - b}{2a - 5} = \frac{9 + b}{10 - 2a}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Cross-multiply to clear the fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (-9 - b)(10 - 2a) = (9 + b)(2a - 5)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Expand both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -90 - 20a - 10b + 2ab = 18a - 45 + 2ab + 5b
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -90 - 10b - 2ab + 45 = 18a - 45 + 2ab
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -45 - 10b - 2ab = 18a - 45
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract \(-45\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -10b - 2ab = 18a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Divide by \(-1\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 10b + 2ab = -18a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Divide by \(2a\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5b + ab = -9a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Factor out \(a\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a(5 + b) = -9a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a = -\frac{9a}{5 + b}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a = \frac{9}{5 + b}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This equation must hold for all \(b\), so we can choose \(b = 3\) (a reasonable value):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a = \frac{9}{5 + 3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a = \frac{9}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the ordered pair \((a, b)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\left( \frac{9}{8}, 3 \right)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
