[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} a \\ -1 \\ c \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The cross product \(\mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ a & -1 & c \\ 7 & 3 & 5 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \mathbf{i} \left( (-1)(5) - (c)(3) \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( a(5) - (c)(7) \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( a(3) - (-1)(7) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying the components, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \mathbf{i} (-5 - 3c) - \mathbf{j} (5a - 7c) + \mathbf{k} (3a + 7)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 - 3c \\ 5a - 7c \\ 3a + 7 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We are given that this cross product equals \(\begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ -16 \\ 25 \end{pmatrix}\). Therefore, we can set up the following system of equations:
