[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the area of the curved surface of the right cylinder, we need to use the formula for the curved surface area of a right cylinder. The formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Curved Surface Area} = 2\pi r h
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( r \) is the radius of the cylinder,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( h \) is the height of the cylinder.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The radius \( r \) is 2 inches,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - The height \( h \) is 5 inches.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can substitute these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Curved Surface Area} = 2\pi (2) (5)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we multiply the radius by the height:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 \times 2 \times 5 = 20
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we multiply the result by \(\pi\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 20\pi
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the area of the curved surface of the cylinder is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{20\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
