[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A recent study found that 60$\%$ of men and 80$\%$ of women surveyed support increased funding for particular medical research. The study surveyed 100 men and 900 women. What was the overall percent of the people surveyed who supported increased funding?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the overall percent of the people surveyed who supported increased funding, we can use the principle of independent probabilities to calculate the combined support. 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Identify the total number of participants surveyed:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    100 \text{ men} + 900 \text{ women} = 1000 \text{ participants}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Identify the individual support rates:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - 60 $\%$ of men support increased funding:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      0.60 \times 1000 = 600 \text{ men}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - 80 $\%$ of women support increased funding:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      0.80 \times 900 = 720 \text{ women}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Use the principle of independent probabilities to find the overall support rate:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Overall support rate} = 0.60 \times 720 + 0.80 \times 600
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Calculate the individual support for men and women:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Men: \(600\) and Women: \(720\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. Perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    0.60 \times 720 = 432
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    0.80 \times 600 = 480
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. Sum the accommodated total:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    432 + 480 = 912
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 7. Finally, calculate the overall percent of supporters:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{912}{1000} \times 100\% = 91.2\%
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the overall percent of the people surveyed who supported increased funding is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{91.2\%}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
