[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To evaluate \(\log_3 \frac{1}{3}\), we need to determine what power of 3 will give us \(\frac{1}{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's set up the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \log_3 \frac{1}{3} = x
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This means we need to find \(x\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^x = \frac{1}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we express \(\frac{1}{3}\) as a power of 3:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{1}{3} = 3^{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3^x = 3^{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the bases are the same, we can set the exponents equal to each other:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x = -1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\log_3 \frac{1}{3}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
