[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If $x$, $y$, and $z$ are real numbers for which  \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x+y-z &= -8, \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x-y+z &= 18,\text{ and} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -x+y+z &= 30, \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{align*} then what is $xyz$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the system of equations and find \(xyz\), we start with the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. \(x + y - z = -8\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. \(x - y + z = 18\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. \(-x + y + z = 30\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's add all three equations together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x + y - z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) = -8 + 18 + 30
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying the left side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y - z + x - y + z - x + y + z = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So the left side simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y + z = 20
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we have the simplified system:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. \(x + y - z = -8\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. \(x - y + z = 18\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. \(x + y + z = 20\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we add the first and fourth equations together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (x + y - z) + (x + y + z) = -8 + 20
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2x + 2y = 12 \implies x + y = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we have the simplified system:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. \(x + y - z = -8\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. \(x + y + z = 20\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. \(x + y = 6\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m From the third equation, we can express \(x + y\) in terms of \(z\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y = 6 \implies x = 6 - y
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute \(x = 6 - y\) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (6 - y) + y + z = 20 \implies 6 + z = 20 \implies z = 14
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now substitute \(x = 6 - y\) back into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (6 - y) + y - z = -8 \implies 6 - z = -8 \implies z = 14
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We have \(x = 6 - y\) and \(z = 14\). To verify, we substitute these values back into any of the original equations. Using the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m x + y - z = -(6 - y) + y - 14 = -6 + y + y - 14 = -20 + 2y = -8
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Solving for \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2y = -6 \implies y = -3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Then \(x = 6 - (-3) = 9\). Finally, \(z = 14\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, \(x = 9\), \(y = -3\), and \(z = 14\). Notice that \(xyz = 9 \cdot (-3) \cdot 14 = -378\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{-378}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
