[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Substitute \( b = 3a \) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    16a + 4(3a) + c = 0 \implies 16a + 12a + c = 0 \implies 28a + c = 0 \implies c = -28a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. **Find the value of \( a \):**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We need to find a common \( a \) that satisfies all equations. We can use the original system directly to find \( a \) and \( b \). From \( 3a = b \) and \( b = 3a \), we get \( b = 3a \). Substituting \( b = 3a \) into another equation, we can use the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    25a + 5(3a) + c = -36 \implies 25a + 15a + c = -36 \implies 40a + c = -36
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Substitute \( b = 3a \) into \( 40a + c = -36 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    40a + c = -36 \implies c = -36 - 40a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    From \( b = 3a \) and \( c = -36 - 40a \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    c = -36 - 40a
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We can choose \( a = 1 \) to find \( b \) and \( c \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    b = 3(1) = 3 \quad \text{and} \quad c = -36 - 40(1) = -36 - 40 = -76
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
