[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify the expression \((9 \times 10^8) \div (3 \times 10^3)\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Separate the numerical coefficients and the powers of 10:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \frac{9 \times 10^8}{3 \times 10^3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Divide the numerical coefficients:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    9 \div 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Simplify the powers of 10:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    10^8 \div 10^3 = 10^{8-3} = 10^5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Combine the results from steps 2 and 3:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    3 \times 10^5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the simplified form of the expression \((9 \times 10^8) \div (3 \times 10^3)\) is \(\boxed{3000000}\).<|endoftext|>
