[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Find the $3 \times 3$ matrix $\mathbf{M}$ such that
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} = -4 \mathbf{v}\]for all three-dimensional vectors $\mathbf{v}.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the $3 \times 3$ matrix $\mathbf{M}$ such that $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} = -4 \mathbf{v}$ for all three-dimensional vectors $\mathbf{v}$, we can express $\mathbf{v}$ in terms of its components:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \\ x_3 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting these into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix} = -4 \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -4a \\ -4b \\ -4c \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find $\mathbf{M}$, we can express the components of $\mathbf{M}$ in terms of the components of $\mathbf{v}$:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\ 0 & -4 & 1 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 6 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\ 0 & -4 & 1 \end{pmatrix}}.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The third column of the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ is all ones, which means $\mathbf{M}$ is the identity matrix. Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{\text{The identity matrix}}$.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -4 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
