[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A rectangular prism has dimensions 8 inches by 2 inches by 32 inches. If a cube has the same volume as the prism, what is the surface area of the cube, in square inches?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the surface area of the cube, we first need to find the volume of the rectangular prism. The volume of a rectangular prism is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Volume} = \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{height} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For our prism, the dimensions are 8 inches, 2 inches, and 32 inches. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Volume} = 8 \, \text{inches} \times 2 \, \text{inches} \times 32 \, \text{inches} = 512 \, \text{cubic inches} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The cube has the same volume as the rectangular prism, so the volume of the cube is also 512 cubic inches. The volume of a cube is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Volume} = \text{side}^3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's denote the side length of the cube by \( s \). Then we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ s^3 = 512 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \( s \), we take the cube root of both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ s = \sqrt[3]{512} = 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The surface area of a cube is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Surface Area} = 6 \times \text{side}^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting \( s = 8 \) into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Surface Area} = 6 \times 8^2 = 6 \times 64 = 384 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the surface area of the cube is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{384} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 384
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m True
