[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the distance from the center to the chord is 2 inches, we can use the properties of the circle to confirm this.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In a circle, any angle subtended by the same arc is equal to the arc itself. If we draw the perpendicular from the center to the chord, the radius forms a right triangle with the midpoint of the chord and the center, and the angle at the center is $120^\circ$ because the chord is subtended by an arc of 60 degrees (since the angle subtended at the center by an arc is twice the angle at the circumference subtending the same arc). Thus, the length of the chord is $2 \sin(30^\circ) = 2 \cdot \frac{1}{2} = 1$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
