[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify the expression \(\frac{11!}{9! + 2 \cdot 8!}\), we will follow a step-by-step approach.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's write out the factorials involved:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(11!\) (11 factorial) is the same as \(11 \times 10 \times 9!\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(9!\) is the factorial of 9, which is \(9 \times 8!\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(2 \cdot 8!\) is twice the value of \(8!\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, we can rewrite the expression as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{11!}{9! + 2 \cdot 8!} = \frac{11 \times 10 \times 9!}{9! + 2 \times 8!}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, let's simplify the denominator \(9! + 2 \cdot 8!\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9! = 9 \times 8!
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 \cdot 8! = 2 \times 8! \times 8!
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the denominator becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9! + 2 \cdot 8! = 9 \times 8! + 2 \times 8! \times 8!
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Factor out \(8!\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9 \times 8! + 2 \times 8! \times 8! = 8!(9 + 2 \times 8!) = 8!(9 + 16) = 8! \times 25
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute this back into the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{11 \times 10 \times 9!}{9! + 2 \cdot 8!} = \frac{11 \times 10 \times 9!}{8! \times 25}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, simplify the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 11 \times 10 \times 9! = 930 \times 9!
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute this back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{930 \times 9!}{8! \times 25} = \frac{930 \times 9!}{8! \times 25}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Notice that \(9!\) is the same as \(9 \times 8!\), so we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{930 \times 9!}{8! \times 25} = \frac{930 \times 8! \times 9!}{8! \times 25} = \frac{930 \times 9!}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{930 \times 9!}{25} = 930 \times \frac{9!}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since \(9! = 9 \times 8!\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 930 \times \frac{9!}{25} = 930 \times \frac{9 \times 8!}{25} = 930 \times \frac{9}{25} \times 8! = 930 \times 0.36 \times 8! = 329.52
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the simplified form of the expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{329.52}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
