[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the eleventh number in the list of positive integers whose digits add up to 11, we start by identifying the digits and considering the constraints for the number to be a 3-digit number (since \(11\) is a single digit and \(29\) and \(38\) are even, the only possibilities for three digits are \(29, 11, 11\)).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. For \(111\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(1 + 1 + 1 = 3\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. For \(291\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(2 + 9 + 1 = 12\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. For \(381\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(3 + 8 + 1 = 12\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. For \(471\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(4 + 7 + 1 = 12\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 5. For \(1111\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4\), which is less than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6. For \(292\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(2 + 9 + 2 = 13\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 7. For \(382\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(3 + 8 + 2 = 13\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 8. For \(472\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(4 + 7 + 2 = 13\), which is more than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9. For \(1112\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The sum of the digits is \(1 + 1 + 1 + 2 = 5\), which is less than 11.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the only three-digit numbers that add up to more than 11 are \(1111\) and \(292\) (which is \(100 + 12 = 112\)), the eleventh number in the list is \(1112\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the answer is \(\boxed{1112}\).<|endoftext|>
