[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplify $\cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Enter your answer is a trigonometric function evaluated at an integer, such as "sin 7".  (The system will assume that the angle is in degrees.)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify the expression \(\cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ\), we will use some trigonometric identities and properties of cosine.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's use the identity for the cosine of a difference:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos(A - B) = \cos A \cos B + \sin A \sin B
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If we let \(A = 54^\circ\) and \(B = 4^\circ\), then:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ = \cos(54^\circ - 4^\circ) = \cos 50^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we will use the fact that \(\cos x = \sin(\frac{\pi}{2} - x)\) to rewrite \(\cos 50^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos 50^\circ = \sin(\frac{\pi}{2} - 50^\circ) = \sin(50^\circ - \pi)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Using the identity \(\sin(\theta - \pi) = -\sin(\theta)\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \sin(50^\circ - \pi) = \sin(50^\circ - 180^\circ) = -\sin(50^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos 50^\circ = -\sin(50^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ = -\sin(50^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, we convert back to degrees:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -\sin(50^\circ) = -\sin(50^\circ - 90^\circ) = -\sin(-40^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Using the property of sine that \(\sin(-x) = -\sin(x)\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m -\sin(-40^\circ) = \sin(40^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the simplified form of the expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{\sin 40}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
