[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For each value of $x,$ $f(x)$ is defined to be the minimum value of the three numbers $2x + 2,$ $\frac{1}{2} x + 1,$ and $-\frac{3}{4} x + 7.$  Find the maximum value of $f(x).$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the maximum value of the function \( f(x) \) defined by the inequalities \( 2x + 2 \leqslant (1/2)x + 1 \leqslant -\frac{3}{4}x + 7 \), we will first determine the ranges of the endpoints of the inequalities.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Starting with the first inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 2x + 2 \leqslant (1/2)x + 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract \( (1/2)x \) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 2x - (1/2)x \leqslant 1 - 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 3/2x \leqslant -1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Multiply both sides by 2/3 to isolate \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ x \leqslant -\frac{2}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the first endpoint is \( x = -\frac{2}{3} \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, consider the second inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ (1/2)x + 1 \leqslant -\frac{3}{4}x + 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Subtract \( -\frac{3}{4}x \) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ (1/2)x + \frac{3}{4}x \leqslant 7 - 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \frac{7}{4}x \leqslant 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Multiply both sides by 4/7:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ x \leqslant \frac{24}{7} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the second endpoint is \( x = \frac{24}{7} \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the maximum value of \( f(x) \), we need to find the value of \( x \) that maximizes the distance between the points \( x \leqslant -\frac{2}{3} \), \( -\frac{2}{3} \leqslant x \leqslant \frac{24}{7} \), and \( x = \frac{24}{7} \). The distance between \( x \leqslant -\frac{2}{3} \) and \( x = \frac{24}{7} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \left( -\frac{2}{3} - \frac{24}{7} \right) \text{ units} = \left( -\frac{14}{21} - \frac{60}{21} \right) = -\frac{74}{21} \text{ units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The distance between a point \( x \leqslant -\frac{2}{3} \) and \( x = \frac{24}{7} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \left( \frac{24}{7} - \left( -\frac{2}{3} \right) \right) \text{ units} = \left( \frac{24}{7} + \frac{14}{7} \right) = \frac{38}{7} \text{ units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To maximize the distance, we need to find a common point \( x \) that lies exactly on the line segment connecting \( x = \frac{24}{7} \) and \( x = -\frac{2}{3} \). The midpoint of the line segment connecting \( x = \frac{24}{7} \) and \( x = -\frac{2}{3} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ x = \frac{\frac{24}{7} + \left( -\frac{2}{3} \right)}{2} = \frac{\frac{24}{7} - \frac{14}{21}}{2} = \frac{\frac{72}{21} - \frac{14}{21}}{2} = \frac{\frac{58}{21}}{2} = \frac{58}{42} = \frac{29}{21} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Evaluating the function at \( x = \frac{29}{21} \) and \( x = \frac{24}{7} \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f\left( \frac{29}{21} \right) = \left( \frac{29}{21} \leq -\frac{2}{3} \right) - \left( \frac{29}{21} \leq \frac{24}{7} \right) + \left( \frac{29}{21} = \frac{11}{21} \right) = \frac{11}{21} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ f\left( \frac{24}{7} \right) = (2)(-\frac{2}{3}) + (2/2)(\frac{24}{7}) + (7/2)(\frac{29}{21}) + 2 \cdot (-\frac{2}{3}) + \frac{1}{2}(29/27) + 2 \cdot (2/7) + (2/7) \left( \frac{24}{7} \right) + (-\frac{3}{4})(29/27) + 7 \left( \frac{29}{21} \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ = -\frac{4}{3} + \frac{29}{7} + \frac{29}{5} - \frac{2}{9} + \frac{3}{9} + \frac{4}{7} + \frac{13}{21} - \frac{29}{27} + \left( 6 - \frac{1}{7} \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ = -\frac{8}{21} + \frac{126}{21} + \frac{58}{35} - \frac{2}{27} + \frac{42}{105} + \frac{35}{105} + \frac{13}{21} - \frac{29}{27} + \frac{126}{21} - \frac{5}{27} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ = \frac{76}{21} + \frac{126}{21} + \frac{58}{35} - \frac{2}{27} + \frac{77}{105} + \frac{35}{105} + \frac{13}{21} - \frac{29}{27} + \frac{126}{21} - \frac{5}{27} = \frac{240}{21} + \frac{126}{21} + \frac{58}{35} - \frac{2}{27} + \frac{77}{105} + \frac{35}{105} + \frac{13}{21} - \frac{29}{27} + \frac{126}{21} - \frac{5}{27} = \frac{360}{21} + \frac{126}{21} + \frac{58}{35} - \frac{2}{27} + \frac{81.33}{105} + \frac{28.33}{105} + \frac{13}{21} - \frac{29}{27} + \frac{126}{21} - \frac{5}{27} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ = \frac{786 + 7188.8 + 580 - 14 + 253.3 + 280.8}{765} = \frac{8430.8}{765} \approx 10.68 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The maximum value of \( f(x) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{1} \]<|endoftext|>
