[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    73 < 80
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    This is true, so \( x = 73 \) is indeed the largest integer less than 80 that satisfies the condition.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the largest integer less than 80 that leaves a remainder of 3 when divided by 5 is:
