[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since we are given that the complement of angle \( M \) is 10 degrees, we can substitute 10 for the complement of \( M \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 90^\circ - M = 10^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we solve for \( M \) by isolating it on one side of the equation. We do this by subtracting 10 from 90:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
