[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve for \(abc\) given the equations \(ab + 4b = -16\), \(bc + 4c = -16\), and \(ca + 4a = -16\), we can start by expressing \(bc + 4c = -16\) in a more convenient form. We can do this by adding \(4c\) to both sides of the equation:
