[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \(\frac{p}{p-a} + \frac{q}{q-b} + \frac{r}{r-c}\), we can use the fact that the simplified expression is always zero. This is because the terms involving \(a\), \(b\), \(c\), \(p\), \(q\), and \(r\) cancel each other out in the context of the equation.
