[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Determine which of these numbers can be a perfect square or cube.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Calculate the sum of all such cubes.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The smallest three-digit number is 100, and the largest is 999. We will check each number from 100 to 999 to see if it is a perfect cube or a perfect square.
