[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Find the product of the least common multiple (LCM) of $8$ and $6$ and the greatest common divisor (GCD) of $8$ and $6$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the least common multiple (LCM) of \( 8 \) and \( 6 \), we use the relationship between the LCM and the GCD of two numbers. Specifically, for any two integers \( a \) and \( b \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{LCM}(a, b) \times \text{GCD}(a, b) = a \times b
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, for \( a = 8 \) and \( b = 6 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{LCM}(8, 6) \times \text{GCD}(8, 6) = 8 \times 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we calculate the LCM and the GCD of \( 8 \) and \( 6 \). The prime factorization of \( 8 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 8 = 2^3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The prime factorization of \( 6 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 = 2 \times 3
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{LCM}(8, 6) = 2^3 \times 3 = 8 \times 3 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The GCD is found by taking the lowest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations. 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{GCD}(8, 6) = 2^1 \times 3^1 = 2 \times 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we use these values to verify the LCM and GCD:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{LCM}(8, 6) = 24
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{GCD}(8, 6) = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Finally, we calculate the product of the LCM and the GCD:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{LCM}(8, 6) \times \text{GCD}(8, 6) = 24 \times 6 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{144}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
