[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m You are a great help, and here is a possible (yet insufficient) solution:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \sqrt[3]{x} + \sqrt{x+12} &= 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Let's introduce a substitution:} &\quad a = \sqrt[3]{x}, \quad b = \sqrt{x+12} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Substituting these into the equation:} &\quad a + b &= 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Rewriting, we have:} &\quad a + b = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Multiplying both sides by 3:} &\quad 3a + 3b = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Simplifying this, we get:} &\quad 3(a + b) = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Since } a + b = 0, \text{ the only solution is:} &\quad a = -b \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Substituting back, we get:} &\quad a + b = -b \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Simplifying this, we have:} &\quad 2a = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{This gives us:} &\quad a = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Since } a = \sqrt[3]{x}, \text{ we then have:} &\quad \sqrt[3]{x} = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{Cubing both sides of the equation:} &\quad x = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
