[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m What is the value of $9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1$?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the value of \(9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1\), let's break it down step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Calculate \(9^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    9^2 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    9^3 = 9 \times 81 = 729
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Calculate \(3 \times 9^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    3 \times 81 = 243
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Calculate \(3 \times 9\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    3 \times 9 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, substitute these values back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1 = 729 + 243 + 27 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Add the numbers together:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    729 + 243 = 972
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    972 + 27 = 999
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    999 + 1 = 1000
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \(9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1\) is \(\boxed{1000}\).<|endoftext|>
