[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To convert the base-6 number \(54321_6\) to a base-10 number, we need to understand the place values in base-6. In base-6, the rightmost digit represents \(6^0\) (or 1), the next digit to the left represents \(6^1\) (or 6), the next represents \(6^2\) (or 36), the next represents \(6^3\) (or 216), and so on.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given the number \(54321_6\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Identify the place values:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The rightmost digit is \(1\), which represents \(6^0\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The next digit to the left is \(4\), which represents \(6^1\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The next digit to the left is \(3\), which represents \(6^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The next digit is \(2\), which represents \(6^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - The leftmost digit is \(5\), which represents \(6^4\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Write the number in terms of these place values:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    54321_6 = 5 \cdot 6^4 + 4 \cdot 6^3 + 3 \cdot 6^2 + 2 \cdot 6^1 + 1 \cdot 6^0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. Calculate each term:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    5 \cdot 6^4 = 5 \cdot 1296 = 6480
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    4 \cdot 6^3 = 4 \cdot 216 = 864
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    3 \cdot 6^2 = 3 \cdot 36 = 108
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2 \cdot 6^1 = 2 \cdot 6 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    1 \cdot 6^0 = 1 \cdot 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. Add these values together to get the base-10 equivalent:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    6480 + 864 + 108 + 12 + 1 = 7555
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the base-10 equivalent of \(54321_6\) is \(\boxed{7555}\).<|endoftext|>
