[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To compute the determinant of the given 2x2 matrix, we use the formula for the determinant of a 2x2 matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{det}(A) = ad - bc
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(a\) and \(b\) are the elements of the top row,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(c\) and \(d\) are the elements of the bottom row.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For the matrix \(\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ 3 & 5 \end{pmatrix}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(a = 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(b = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(c = 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \(d = 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute these values into the determinant formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{det}\left(\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ 3 & 5 \end{pmatrix}\right) = (0)(5) - (1)(3)
