[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the common ratio of the infinite geometric series \(\frac{-3}{5} - \frac{5}{3} - \frac{125}{27} - \dots\), we need to identify the ratio between consecutive terms.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's express each term in the series in a general form:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a_1 = \frac{-3}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a_2 = \frac{-5}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m a_3 = \frac{-125}{27}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The common ratio \(r\) is the quotient of any term and the preceding term. So, we calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m r = \frac{a_2}{a_1} = \frac{\frac{-5}{3}}{\frac{-3}{5}} = \frac{-5}{3} \cdot \frac{5}{-3} = \frac{-5 \cdot 5}{3 \cdot -3} = \frac{-25}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To ensure accuracy, let's check with \(r = \frac{a_3}{a_2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m r = \frac{a_3}{a_2} = \frac{\frac{-125}{27}}{\frac{-5}{3}} = \frac{-125}{27} \cdot \frac{3}{-5} = \frac{-125 \cdot 3}{27 \cdot -5} = \frac{-375}{135} = \frac{-25}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since both calculations yield the same ratio:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m r = \frac{-25}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
