[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve this problem, let's use some geometric properties and algebraic steps. We are given that $\triangle CBD$ has a perimeter of $19$ and $\triangle ABC$ has a perimeter of $20$. We also know that $BD = 7$ and $BC = 8$. Since both triangles are isosceles, we can use their base angles to set up equations.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, let's denote the lengths of the sides as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $AB = DC = c$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $BC = BD + CD = 7 + c$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $AC = AD + CD = 8 + c$ (since $\triangle ABC$ has a perimeter of 20, we have $2c = 20 - 7 = 13$, so $c = 6.5$). Thus, $AC = 6.5 + c = 6.5 + 6.5 = 13$. (We used the fact that the perimeter of $\triangle ABC$ is 20 to find the value of $c$.)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we know the sides of $\triangle ABD$, $\triangle BCD$, $\triangle CBD$, $\triangle CDA$, and $\triangle ADC$:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - AB = 6.5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - BD = 7
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - CD = 6.5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $CD = 8 + c$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - DA = 8 - c
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Using the fact that the sum of the angles in a triangle is $180^\circ$, we can find the angles of $\triangle ABD$:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle ADB = \angle ADC = 70^\circ$ because $\angle ABD = \angle ACD = 40^\circ$. So, $\angle DAB = 50^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m And similarly for $\triangle BCD$:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \angle BDC = 40^\circ, \angle BCA = 40^\circ, \angle BCA = 40^\circ, \angle DBC = 40^\circ. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we need to find $\angle ADB$ and $\angle BDC$:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle ADB = 50^\circ$, so $\angle CBD = 50^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle BDC = 40^\circ$, so $\angle CBD = 40^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle DAB = 50^\circ$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle DBC = 40^\circ$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle CBD = 50^\circ$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know these angles sum to $180^\circ$:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 50^\circ + 40^\circ + 50^\circ + 50^\circ = 180^\circ. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m But we also know:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \angle BDC = \angle DBC = 40^\circ \text{ and } \angle DCA = 40^\circ. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \angle ABD = \angle BDA + \angle ABD = (50^\circ + 40^\circ) - 40^\circ = 60^\circ. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [asy]
