[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to verify our solution by calculating the other angles and checking if the perimeter is correct:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle ADB = 50^\circ$, $\angle CBD = 50^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - $\angle BDC = 40^\circ$, $\angle BDA = 40^\circ$, $\angle CAN = 20^\circ$ and $\angle DAB = 60^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Adding these up, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 50^\circ + 50^\circ + 40^\circ + 60^\circ = 180^\circ. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, our solution is correct. The length of $AB$ is \(\boxed{6.5}\).<|endoftext|>
