[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If $\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{vmatrix} = 5,$ then find
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[\begin{vmatrix} a - c & b - d \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the determinant of the matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} a - c & b - d \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}\), we use the formula for the determinant of a 2x2 matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} p & q \\ r & s \end{vmatrix} = ps - qr\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, we identify the elements of the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \begin{vmatrix} a - c & b - d \\ c & d \end{vmatrix} = d(d - c) - c(b - d). \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We will expand this expression step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. Expand \(d(d - c)\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ d(d - c) = d^2 - dc. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. Expand \(-c(b - d)\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ -c(b - d) = -cb + cd. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, substitute these expansions back into the determinant formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ d(d - c) - c(b - d) = d^2 - dc - cb + cd. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the \(cd\) terms cancel each other out, we are left with:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ d^2 - cb. \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the determinant of the matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{d^2 - cb}. \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
