[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \( f(3) \) given the functions \( f(x) = g(g(x)) - g(x) \) and \( g(x) = 2x - 1 \), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Find \( g(3) \)**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Given \( g(x) = 2x - 1 \), substitute \( x = 3 \) to find \( g(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    g(3) = 2(3) - 1 = 6 - 1 = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Find \( f(3) \)**:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Substitute \( g(3) = 5 \) into the function \( f(x) = g(g(x)) - g(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    f(3) = g(g(3)) - g(3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We already know \( g(3) = 5 \), so we need to find \( g(5) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    g(5) = 2(5) - 1 = 10 - 1 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Now substitute \( g(5) = 9 \) into the expression for \( f(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    f(3) = 9 - 5 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( f(3) \) is \(\boxed{4}\).<|endoftext|>
