[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how much money is in Alan's bank account after 10 years, we need to use the formula for compound interest. The formula for the amount \( A \) after time \( t \) with an annual interest rate \( r \) compounded annually is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A = P \left(1 + r\right)^t
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( P \) is the principal amount (the initial amount of money),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( r \) is the annual interest rate (in decimal form),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( t \) is the time the money is invested for in years.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In this problem:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( P = 500 \) dollars,
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( r = 0.03 \) (since 3 percent is 0.03 when expressed as a decimal),
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m - \( t = 10 \) years.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substitute these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A = 500 \left(1 + 0.03\right)^{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m First, calculate \( 1 + 0.03 \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 + 0.03 = 1.03
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, raise 1.03 to the power of 10:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1.03^{10} \approx 1.21583463
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, multiply this result by the principal amount:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A \approx 500 \times 1.21583463 \approx 607.917315
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since we need the amount to the nearest dollar, we round 607.917315 to the nearest dollar:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m A \approx 608
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, after 10 years, the amount in Alan's bank account is \(\boxed{608}\).<|endoftext|>
