[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Identify the number of sides of each triangle**: Each pentagon can be divided into 5 smaller triangles by drawing lines from the center of the pentagon to each of the vertices.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Count the number of triangles**: The number of triangles in a pentagon is 5. Since each triangle contributes 3 to the perimeter of the polygon (as one vertex of each triangle is connected to the center and a vertex of the polygon), the total number of unit squares in the polygon is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
