[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Next, we consider the denominator \(\cos ^{2} \sqrt[3]{x}\). As \(x\) approaches 1, \(\cos \sqrt[3]{x}\) approaches \(\cos 1\), which is a value between 0 and 1. Therefore, \(\cos ^{2} \sqrt[3]{x}\) approaches 0 but is slightly greater than 0. So, the denominator is a very small positive number.
