[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Adjust for the overlapping items:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - From the diagram, it seems that some items are counted twice: 10 common items in \( A \cap B \), and 2 others which are in circle \( B \) (but not in \( C \)).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    - Therefore, the number of items in \( B \) but not in \( C \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Number of items in } B \text{ but not in } C = \text{Total items in } B - \text{Items in } B \cap C = 10 - 10 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the number of items in \( B \) but not in \( C \) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
