[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The volume of the parallelepiped generated by $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix},$ $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}$ is 15.  Find $k,$ where $k > 0.$
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \( k \) for which the volume of the parallelepiped generated by the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix},\) \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix},\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}\) is 15. The volume of the parallelepiped formed by vectors \(\mathbf{u},\) \(\mathbf{v},\) and \(\mathbf{w}\) is given by the absolute value of the scalar triple product \(\mathbf{u} \cdot(\mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{w}).\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Given vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The scalar triple product is calculated as:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot(\mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{w}) = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 & 3 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 & k & 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Expanding the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2 & 3 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1 & k & 2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{vmatrix} = \mathbf{i} \left(3 \cdot 2 - 4 \cdot k\right) - \mathbf{j} \left(2 \cdot 2 - 4 \cdot 1\right) + \mathbf{k} \left(2 \cdot k - 3 \cdot 1\right)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \mathbf{i} (6 - 4k) - \mathbf{j} (4 - 4) + \mathbf{k} (2k - 3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \mathbf{i} (6 - 4k) + \mathbf{k} (2k - 3)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 6 - 4k \\ 2k - 3 \\ 2k - 3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The volume of the parallelepiped is the absolute value of the scalar triple product:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m | \begin{pmatrix} 6 - 4k \\ 2k - 3 \\ 2k - 3 \end{pmatrix} | = 15
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Taking the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m | \begin{pmatrix} 6 - 4k \\ 2k - 3 \\ 2k - 3 \end{pmatrix} | = \sqrt{(6 - 4k)^2 + (2k - 3)^2 + (2k - 3)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying inside the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{(6 - 4k)^2 + (2k - 3)^2 + (2k - 3)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{(6 - 4k)^2 + (4k^2 - 12k + 9) + (4k^2 - 12k + 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{(6 - 4k)^2 + (4k^2 - 12k + 9) + (4k^2 - 12k + 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = \sqrt{(6 - 4k)^2 + (4k^2 - 12k + 9) + (4k^2 - 12k + 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We know that the volume is 15, so:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m | \begin{pmatrix} 6 - 4k \\ 2k - 3 \\ 2k - 3 \end{pmatrix} | = \sqrt{15} \implies 6 - 4k + 2k - 3 + 2k - 3 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, \(6 - 4k + 2k - 3 + 2k - 3 = 0\), which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 - 4k + 2k - 3 + 2k - 3 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the value of \( k \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{1}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{9}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
