[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Harry, Ron and Neville are having a race on their broomsticks.  If there are no ties, in how many different possible orders can they finish?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the number of different possible orders in which Harry, Ron, and Neville can finish their race, we need to calculate the number of permutations of the three individuals. A permutation is an arrangement of all the members of a set into some sequence or order.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The formula to find the number of permutations of \( n \) distinct objects is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m n! \quad \text{(n factorial)}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \( n! \) represents the product of all positive integers up to \( n \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m In this case, \( n = 3 \) (since there are 3 individuals: Harry, Ron, and Neville). Therefore, we need to calculate \( 3! \):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3! = 3 \times 2 \times 1
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, let's perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3 \times 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6 \times 1 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the number of different possible orders in which Harry, Ron, and Neville can finish is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{6}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 6
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
