[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine how many of the natural numbers from 1 to 600 inclusive contain the digit 5 at least once, we will break down the problem by considering the occurrences of the digit 5 in each digit place (units, tens, hundreds, and thousands) separately.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 1: Count the number of times 5 appears in the units place
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The numbers from 1 to 600 that end in 5 are: 500, 501, 502, 503, 504, 505, 506, 507, 508, 509, 510, 511, 512, 513, 514, 515, 516, 517, 518, 519, 520, 521, 522, 523, 524, 525, 526, 527, 528, 529, 530, 531, 532, 533, 534, 535, 536, 537, 538, 539, 540, 541, 542, 543, 544, 545, 546, 547, 548, 549, 550, 551, 552, 553, 554, 555, 556, 557, 558, 559, 560, 561, 562, 563, 564, 565, 566, 567, 568, 569, 570, 571, 572, 573, 574, 575, 576, 577, 578, 579, 580, 581, 582, 583, 584, 585, 586, 587, 588, 589, 590, 591, 592, 593, 594, 595, 596, 597, 598, 599. There are 35 numbers ending in 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 2: Count the number of times 5 appears in the tens place
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The numbers from 1 to 600 that end in 5 are: 515, 525, 535, 545, 555, 565, 575, 585, 595, 605, 615, 625, 635, 645, 655, 665, 675, 685, 695, 705, 715, 725, 735, 745, 755, 765, 775, 785, 795, 805, 815, 825, 835, 845, 855, 865, 875, 885, 895. There are 35 numbers ending in 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 3: Count the number of times 5 appears in the hundreds place
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m There are no numbers in the form 000-050 that end in 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 4: Count the number of times 5 appears in the thousands place
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The only number in the form 000-600 that ends in 5 is 550, so there is 1 number.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m ### Step 5: Calculate the total number of numbers that contain the digit 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion, the total number of numbers from 1 to 600 that contain the digit 5 is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 35 + 35 - 1 = 74
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the number of natural numbers from 1 to 600 that contain the digit 5 at least once is \(\boxed{74}\).<|endoftext|>
