[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the 39th digit in the decimal representation of \(\frac{1}{19}\), we first need to determine the repeating decimal pattern of \(\frac{1}{19}\).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The decimal representation of \(\frac{1}{19}\) is a repeating decimal. We perform the division \(1 \div 19\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{array}{r|l}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 19 & 1.000000\ldots \\
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m When we divide \(100\) by \(19\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1.000000\ldots = 100 \div 19 \approx 5.263157894736842
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The integer part is 5, which is the first digit after the decimal point. We subtract \(5 \times 19 = 95\) from \(100\) to get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 100 - 95 = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The integer part is 5, which is the next digit. We subtract \(5 \times 19 = 95\) from \(100\) again to get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 100 - 95 = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This pattern repeats. Hence, the decimal representation of \(\frac{1}{19}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0.\overline{526315} = 0.5263152631526315\ldots
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We need to identify the digit at the 39th position in this repeating sequence. Since the repeating block starts with "526315", we count it step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 0.\overline{526315} \implies 0.\overline{526315} \implies 0.\overline{01526315} \implies 0.\overline{526315}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The 39th digit is "1". Therefore, the 39th digit in the decimal representation of \(\frac{1}{19}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{1}
