[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To compute the product \(\prod_{n = 1}^{20} \frac{n + 3}{n}\), we start by writing out the product explicitly:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \prod_{n = 1}^{20} \frac{n + 3}{n} = \frac{4}{1} \cdot \frac{5}{2} \cdot \frac{6}{3} \cdot \frac{7}{4} \cdot \ldots \cdot \frac{21}{19} \cdot \frac{22}{20}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can rearrange and factor out the common terms \(n + 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \frac{4}{1} \cdot \frac{5}{2} \cdot \frac{6}{3} \cdot \frac{7}{4} \cdot \ldots \cdot \frac{21}{19} \cdot \frac{22}{20} = (4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 \cdot 7 \cdot 8 \cdot 9 \cdot 10 \cdot 11 \cdot 12 \cdot 13 \cdot 14 \cdot 15 \cdot 16 \cdot 17 \cdot 18 \cdot 19 \cdot 20) \cdot \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to compute the product inside the parentheses first. We will list the numbers from 4 to 20 and find the product:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 \cdot 7 \cdot 8 \cdot 9 \cdot 10 \cdot 11 \cdot 12 \cdot 13 \cdot 14 \cdot 15 \cdot 16 \cdot 17 \cdot 18 \cdot 19 \cdot 20
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To simplify this product, we can factor the numbers into primes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4 = 2^2, \quad 5 = 5, \quad 6 = 2 \cdot 3, \quad 7 = 7, \quad 8 = 2^3, \quad 9 = 3^2, \quad 10 = 2 \cdot 5, \quad 11 = 11, \quad 12 = 2^2 \cdot 3, \quad 13 = 13, \quad 14 = 2 \cdot 7, \quad 15 = 3^2 \cdot 5, \quad 16 = 2^4, \quad 17 = 17, \quad 18 = 2 \cdot 3^2, \quad 19 = 19, \quad 20 = 2^2 \cdot 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the product becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2^2 \cdot 5 \cdot (2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2^2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2 \cdot 7) \cdot (2^4) \cdot 11 \cdot (3^2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2^4 \cdot 5) \cdot (2 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2 \cdot 7) \cdot (2 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2^4 \cdot 5) \cdot (2 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 5)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We can see that each pair of terms involving \(2\) and \(3\) are repeated:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2^2 \cdot 5 \cdot (2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 5) \cdot (2 \cdot 3) \cdot (2 \cdot 5) = 2^2 \cdot 5 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdot 2^2 \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 5 = 2^{10} \cdot 3^2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So the product of the remaining terms is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (2^{10} \cdot 3^2) \cdot 11 \cdot 19 \cdot 2 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 5 = (2^{10} \cdot 3^2 \cdot 11 \cdot 19) \cdot 11 \cdot 19
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Notice that \(3^2 \cdot 11 \cdot 19 = 3^2 \cdot 19 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 = 2 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 3 \cdot 11 \cdot 19 = 2 \cdot 3 \cdot 11 \cdot 3 \cdot 19 = 2 \cdot 5 \cdot 11 \cdot 19 = 110 \cdot 19 = 2090\)
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, the product of the remaining terms is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2090 \cdot 11 = 23090
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
