[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since \( BK \) and \( CK \) form a right triangle \( BKC \) with \( BK = \sqrt{5} \) and \( CK = 4 \), we use the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    BK^2 + CK^2 = BC^2
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Substituting the given values:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
