[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For the word "CIRCLE", the word "CIRCLE" consists of 4 letters. The number of permutations of a word with 4 distinct letters is given by \( P(4) \). The formula for permutations is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m P(n) = n! \quad \text{where} \quad n \text{ is the number of letters}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m For our word "CIRCLE", the number of permutations is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
