[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ x^3 - 1 = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since this is generally not true for all \( x \), it seems there might be a misinterpretation or need to re-evaluate the problem. However, based on the given information and standard mathematical techniques, we should consider the specific function form of \( g(x) \) to find \( g^{-1}(f(7)) \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The specific form of \( g(x) \) (not all 3) will need to be considered, but for the sake of this problem, we will assume \( g(x) \) is correctly given and focus on the basic inverse relationship. Given the complexity and the general form, we conclude that \( g^{-1}(f(7)) = 2 \) (as derived from the inverse relationship directly).
