[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{det}\left(\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}\right) = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m The determinant of a 2x2 matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} p & q \\ r & s \end{vmatrix}\) is given by \(ps - qr\). So, for the matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}\):
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \det\left(\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}\right) = ad - bc = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to find the determinant of the new matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \begin{vmatrix} a - c & b - d \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Again, using the determinant formula for a 2x2 matrix, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{det}\left(\begin{vmatrix} a - c & b - d \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}\right) = (a - c)d - (b - d)c
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Substituting the value of what we know from the original determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m (a - c)d - (b - d)c = ad - cd - bc + dc = ad - bc
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m We already known from the original determinant calculation that \(ad - bc = 5\), so:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \text{det}\left(\begin{vmatrix} a - c & b - d \\ c & d \end{vmatrix}\right) = 5
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since both determinants are equal to 5, the determinant of the new matrix is also:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \boxed{5}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m If 10% of a number is 18, what percentage of 46 is 42? To find 10% of a number, we multiply the number by 0.1. So, if 10% of a number is 18, we can calculate the number as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Number = 18 / 0.1 = 180
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now we need to find what percentage of 46 is 42. If 42 is 10% of a number \( x \), then we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ 42 = 0.1 \times x \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find \( x \), we divide both sides of the equation by 0.1:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ x = \frac{42}{0.1} = 42 \times 10 = 420 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, we need to find what percentage of 46 is 42. If we let \( P \) be the percentage we are looking for, then:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P\% = \left( \frac{42}{46} \right) \times 100 \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Simplifying the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \frac{42}{46} = \frac{7}{8} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P\% = \left( \frac{7}{8} \times 100 \right) \% = 87.5\% \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, 10% of a number is 18 when 10% of that number is 18. Now, we need to find what percentage of 46 is 42. Since 42 is 10% of 46, we already calculated this:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ P\% = 87.5\% \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Thus, 87.5% of 46 is 42. The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{87.5} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
