[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m One focus of the ellipse $\frac{x^2}{2} + y^2 = 1$ is at $F = (1,0).$  There exists a point $P = (p,0),$ where $p > 0,$ such that for any chord $\overline{AB}$ that passes through $F,$ angles $\angle APF$ and $\angle BPF$ are equal.  Find $p.$
