[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    2x - px + p - 2 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    This comes from the fact that the tangent at any point on the ellipse \(\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\) at \((x_1, y_1)\) for an angle \(\theta\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    x_1 \tan \theta - y_1 = 0 \quad \Rightarrow \quad y = \frac{x_1}{\tan \theta} = \frac{x_1}{\sqrt{<|endoftext|>
