[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To find the measure of an interior angle of a regular octagon, we can use the formula for the sum of the interior angles of a polygon. The formula is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Sum of interior angles} = (n - 2) \times 180^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m where \( n \) is the number of sides (or vertices) of the polygon. For an octagon, \( n = 8 \). Plugging in the value, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Sum of interior angles} = (8 - 2) \times 180^\circ = 6 \times 180^\circ = 1080^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Now, to find the measure of one interior angle, we divide the sum of the interior angles by the number of sides:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \text{Measure of one interior angle} = \frac{1080^\circ}{8} = 135^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Therefore, the measure of an interior angle of the sign is \(\boxed{135}\) degrees.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
