[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 1. **Identify the total number of three-digit integers between 100 and 500:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    The smallest three-digit number is 100, and the largest is 499.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    499 - 100 + 1 = 390
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    So, there are 390 three-digit integers between 100 and 500.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 2. **Determine the number of three-digit integers that are palindromes:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    A three-digit palindrome reads the same forward and backward, so the first digit must be the same as the last digit, and the second digit must be the same as the second-to-last digit.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Number of palindromic three-digit integers} = 100 + 100 = 200
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 3. **Identify the three-digit integers that contain at least one 5:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    We need to check which of these numbers actually do.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Single-digit number} \equiv 5 \pmod{10}
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    This means the single-digit numbers that include the digit 5 are: 5, 15, 25, 35, 45, 55, 65, 75, 85, 95.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    However, none of these are three-digit numbers using only the digits 0 through 9. Therefore, there are no three-digit integers that contain at least one 5.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 4. **Calculate the percentage of three-digit integers that contain at least one 5:**
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    Since there are no such numbers, the number of three-digit integers that contain at least one 5 is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \text{Percentage} = \left( \frac{0}{390} \right) \times 100 = 0\%
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m    \]
