[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Eight women of different heights are at a party. Each woman decides to only shake hands with women shorter than herself. How many handshakes take place?
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m To determine the number of handshakes that take place, we need to carefully analyze the rule: each woman only shakes hands with women shorter than herself. This means that a woman \( i \) (where \( i \) is an integer from 1 to 8) will shake hands with women \( j \) (where \( j \) is also an integer from 1 to 8, excluding \( i \)).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Since the women are grouped into groups of 2 (i.e., \( j = 1, 3, 5, 7 \)), for any pair of women \( i \) and \( j \) in the same group, \( j \) will always be shorter than \( i \).
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Let's list all the women:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8\} \]
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m Each woman will shake hands with exactly one other woman because the women are grouped into pairs. Therefore, none of the women will shake hands with themselves. The number of handshakes is simply the number of women, which is 8.
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m So, the number of handshakes that take place is:
[36m(main_task pid=251513)[0m \[ \boxed{8} \]<|endoftext|>
